{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot","id":1367740,"title":"Any chance of a Beast rewrite/reboot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-14T06:37:33-08:00","id":1367740,"title":"Any chance of a Beast rewrite/reboot?","content":"I do kind of see a &quot;need&quot; for Beast. Every other game line pretty well covers the classic monster/horror types: vampires, werewolves, ghosts, golems/frankenstein/constructs, faeries, demons and finally mummies. Even Deviant deals with the &quot;person twisted by science/weirdness into a monstrosity like the Invisible man, the Fly, etc.&quot; And Hunter not only deals with the people who hunt monsters, it brings in the idea of the modern slasher types as well (though generally not as PCs). The only thing lacking (beyond full-on extraterrestrials) is the dragon/eldritch monstrosity/mythic monsters that cover everything from sea serpents to shit from Lovecraft. So, yeah, there is kind of a hole there in terms of a monster type, and especially a PC monster type.<br /> <br /> However, the actual game with Hunger and the horrifying abusive shit that must be done to satiate it just sucks every last bit of fun and goodwill out of it for me. It makes wonder if we'll get some spin-off games in the same vein. Perhaps, Stalker: The Pursuit, Rapist: The Ravaging, Batterer: The Bitch-slapping or Pedophile: The Molesting.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, give me a cool way to portray Dragons, Medusas, Sea Serpents or even full-on H.P. Lovecraft weirdies, but please don't make into something like way too many real-life monsters.<br /> <br /> As is, Beast absolutely has a huge crossover aspects in that if a Beast shows up, realistically every other supernatural type will move to destroy it due to the damage it does to all and sundry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T06:53:39-08:00","id":1367745,"title":"","content":"This, give me a game where PC's are born monsters and have to choose either to live as men or beasts. Not edgelord revenge fantasy simulator","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T07:30:58-08:00","id":1367753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367745#post1367745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, give me a game where PC's are born monsters and have to choose either to live as men or beasts. Not edgelord revenge fantasy simulator</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of being rude, how do you propose to make a meaningfully-monstrous monster without making them, well, driven in some way to pursue abhorrent things? If you just take a person and slap on fire-breath, scales and wings, that's a dragon-themed superhero. Not that I wish to denigrate your problems with the gameline - it certainly is very edgy in places - but personally I find the idea of characters driven to monstrous acts interesting, in part <i>because</i> there's no mechanical punishment for doing it, as most of the other gamelines have in their morality meters. The only thing holding you back from becoming a true monster is your moral compass - your own and that of your character. That says something. <br /> <br /> That said, I can see possibility in a paradigm of Hunger or some other equivalent which drives more with carrots than sticks (I'm reminded of the masterful way in which <i>Exalted</i>'s Infernal Charms tempt you to imitate the demon kings by making it so that your powers are simply most effective when doing so - though I'm not calling <i>2e Exalted</i> a masterclass in anything but that). And, let's face it, playing the big mythic monsters is something everyone whose souls haven't been worn down to a funless vestige can get behind. <br /> <br /> On a more practical level, though, wishing for a 'reboot' of Beast at this point is - forgive me - wishful thinking. Perhaps in some glorious future where 3e of CofD has happened and <i>Demon's </i>Pact mechanics aren't as hilariously broken as they presently are, but for the moment I doubt this will be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:22:38-08:00","id":1367767,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, but the skeleton of Beast's design is sound, it just tries to have both a power fantasy and a horror game at the same time and does not strike the balance well. Which is fair, given it's almost impossible to play as both powerful monsters who do monster things and still be sympathetic characters. I can see a couple of solutions that could be explored in a 2e without fundamentally changing the basic skeleton of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T08:25:52-08:00","id":1367768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367767#post1367767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before, but the skeleton of Beast's design is sound, it just tries to have both a power fantasy and a horror game at the same time and does not strike the balance well. Which is fair, given it's almost impossible to play as both powerful monsters who do monster things and still be sympathetic characters. I can see a couple of solutions that could be explored in a 2e without fundamentally changing the basic skeleton of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be curious to hear about your solutions. And I mean that genuinely - I do see the issues with Beast, and I'm an avid homebrewer. Beast isn't too mechanically complex, so there's a reasonable chance of being able to cook up a patch for the thing without throwing the baby out along with the bathwater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:31:56-08:00","id":1367792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367768#post1367768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to hear about your solutions. And I mean that genuinely - I do see the issues with Beast, and I'm an avid homebrewer. Beast isn't too mechanically complex, so there's a reasonable chance of being able to cook up a patch for the thing without throwing the baby out along with the bathwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way to make a monster sympathetic is to give them no good solution to their situation but assume that (at least the PCs!) are trying their best to find the least harmful route. Then you throw drama in the mix and boom, there's a reason this style of game launched two Vampire: The Something franchises.<br /> <br /> I'd divide the life cycle into &quot;Fasting&quot;, &quot;Foraging&quot; and &quot;Feasting.&quot;<br /> <br /> If a Beast deliberately avoids feeding entirely, lives as a human being, they don't fill up their power meters and aren't particularly dangerous in terms of supernatural power. The Horror gets hungry and leaves to hunt in the dream world of the surrounding community. This leads to all kinds of problems and triggers the emergence of Heralds and Heroes. So the most ethical choice on a personal level - not feeding at all - carries with it adverse consequences that are arguably worse for people and certainly more dangerous. Do it long enough, pretend hard enough, and the Beast can almost forget the truth of their condition. Until the first episode of our Beast: The TV Series where the main character gets pulled back in to the horror underground after years away from the life when they discover their Horror caused so many nightmares there was a mass suicide in their home town. So he has to go home, unlock his now dust-covered Lair, and get back into the game.<br /> <br /> The Beast can also Forage, which is feed juuust enough to keep the Horror quiet, but not really enough to be all that powerful. Because the default player character in a World of Darkness game is a private investigator, as an example, say we have a Beast PI who gathers blackmail information and uses the fear created by that to keep their Horror quiet. Still a bad thing to do, but this character is the kind of morally compromised film noir / urban horror / crime drama protagonist everyone's comfortable with playing. You can gather enough power to do monster badass stuff, but not enough so the occupational hazards of a professional blackmailer isn't a problem for you. High end Foraging involves really messing with people, like &quot;bury someone alive, dig them up before they suffocate to feed off the fear&quot; style stuff, but we can expect our player characters not to go that far on a regular basis. But throw in some dramatic necessity to power up and make the victim a tempting target (local mob boss, perhaps) and you could see even PCs going this far.<br /> <br /> This is actually the most dangerous zone and the one that will require lots of negotiation at the table, because many of the &quot;reliable ways of causing a person to experience fear&quot; in the real world are...abusive practices that almost everyone experiences at some point and mostly do not show up as characters we root for in fiction. I chose the blackmailer because at the very least he's picking on people who have already done something and because it's a crime story archetype; WoD urban horror is film noir with fangs most of the time anyway. I say most dangerous because the next level can fit comfortably into the action-fantasy-popcorn-horror style; when John Wick kills a metric ton of mobsters we cheer, but if John Wick was leaving threatening notes on his neighbor's front porch to feed off the resulting anxiety we'd not have any fun.<br /> <br /> Then for our actual monster move, you can Feast, which is straight up bringing someone into your Lair and killing them, monster style. As an example, our private investigator snares people in a web of compromises and blackmail, but in their Lair they are a literal giant spider with literal webs. A hit man hired by one of their victims goes after him, the PI lures him into their Lair, webs him up, and eats him. For PCs, we can assume that going all in like this is a self-defense move, used against bad guy NPCs (action-fantasy-popcorn horror). For a risk/reward, immediately after feeding you are in a food coma and vulnerable, but after some digestion you've filled up your powers. Luring people to their death in a haunted nightmare dimension attracts attention, and you'll be dealing with hunters, monster-slaying Adamantine Arrow, investigating authorities, etc. Beasts who do this to innocent people get got by other beasts, hunters, etc, but for PCs, well, if you lure a group of Russian mobsters into your chicken-legged witch's hut because <i>you're actually Baba Yaga</i> I think we're all fine with this as a character concept.<br /> <br /> Vampire is honest about blood drinking. Beast should be honest about fear harvesting. PCs should absolutely be happy to find those situations where scaring someone is also the right thing to do but they should have to work at finding those &quot;vigilante monster&quot; moments.<br /> <br /> Just admit that these are people who are in a terrible situation and have to do monstrous things to survive. The drama comes with how they bend the curve of monstrosity as much as possible. That's sympathetic and there are lots of ways to keep the player characters on the right side of the morally-ambiguous-protagonist-sympathy bell curve with pretty stock standard urban fantasy tropes. You don't have an easy out, because not feeding causes your Horror to wreck havoc on the collective subconscious. You can feed just a bit but it makes you a slimeball blackmailer. And you can Feast, but how often can you get a squad of mob hit men to raid your decrepit farmhouse on the edge of town so you can eat them with a clear-ish conscience?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basically, the paradigmatic Beast story is something like LA Confidential. Bud White/Ed Exley/Jack Vincennes are not good people, they are each horribly compromised. But we follow those three and root for them because their compromises have a limit; they each hit a point where they say &quot;Oh no, not any further than this.&quot;<br /> <br /> James Ellroy novels in general seem to be Beast in a nutshell; at least how I'd see a less problematic Beast. They're all about morally damaged people finding a line even they won't cross and making a stand. Usually a self-destructive and ultimately unsuccessful stand, but they're compelling protagonists, monstrous as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":".  the lesson digression served no purpose but to make someone real mad at me 02-14-2020, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:05:50-08:00","id":1367798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367792#post1367792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What'd I'd drop entirely is the cultural norm of &quot;lessons&quot; and any semblance of there being a &quot;Greater Good&quot; to Beast actions. The &quot;for your own good&quot; rationalization towards abuse is just about the most off-putting thing Beast introduced. It'd be fine for NPCs-who-are-jerks but as a cultural norm and as an actual setting conceit with grounding in the metaphysics? No thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>To repeat the correction that keeps getting missed or forgotten in this line of discussion:<br /> <br /> It was never about a greater good or &quot;for your own good.&quot; The Begotten culture of lessons has nothing to do with the victims of feeding except that it means they survive the experience more often.<br /> <br /> Beasts are the human-adjacent monsters closest to native to the Temenos, where ideological conflicts play out as literal warfare and Essence is less important than real estate and the particulars of a metaphorical means of affecting change has knock-on effects.<br /> <br /> &quot;As a person with a piece of powerful mental iconography where your soul is, the people around you are learning something from your activities whether you want them to or not, so it's better to keep your hand on the steering wheel in that regard.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is the context in which lesson culture exists \u2014 for the Beast's sake far moreso than for humanity's, in much the same way that Requiem's version of the Masquerade is far less concerned with people knowing that vampires exist than that <i>you</i> are a vampire (and so are the fifteen people pulling strings in the city government and the criminal underworld). To my knowledge, nobody's yet posited that the Masquerade exists for the good of blood dolls and ghouls.<br /> <br /> Beasts are teachers in the sense that they're particularly compelling active storytellers. That doesn't give them moral absolution, it gives them a lever in the collective unconscious that they can't put down, and the game has never pretended otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:14:49-08:00","id":1367800,"title":"","content":"If it keeps getting missed or forgotten, doesn't tell you something about room for a rewrite?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't mean that to be smarmy or anything. I found much of Beast to be incoherent and contradictory, none more than in respect to the &quot;lesson/teacher&quot; aspect. It feels self-serving and a thin attempt to avoid grappling with the logical moral consequences of the Beast condition. If anything, it makes them even more unsympathetic and obnoxious. The distinction you're drawing between Beasts as some kind of necessary evil and Beasts as abusers with a cover story is so subtle I don't see it as having much value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-14-2020, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T11:23:52-08:00","id":1367818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367800#post1367800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it keeps getting missed or forgotten, doesn't tell you something about room for a rewrite?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026I'm just gonna point out that I didn't say anything about the value of a rewrite in response to your repetition of a common assertion of content that doesn't exist and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The distinction you're drawing between Beasts as some kind of necessary evil and Beasts as abusers with a cover story is so subtle I don't see it as having much value. </div> </div> </div>The distinction between &quot;Hey victims, we monsters are doing this to help you&quot; and &quot;Hey monsters, have some care for the bigger picture of your victimizing&quot; is not subtle.<br /> <br /> It has almost nothing to do with the victims besides &quot;leave them alive so you don't lose control of the only part of the narrative you have direct influence over, i.e. your Horror.&quot; This is not a moral element except in the very broad sense that it asserts having control over the consequences of your actions is better than not having control over the consequences of your actions, particularly when the drawbacks of the Begotten condition are almost entirely comprised of unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> &quot;Misinformation outside of the book itself is leading people to persistently fail to actually read the book&quot; is not a thing that speaks to the necessity of a rewrite any more than any other gameline's &quot;there's some stuff that could stand to be clearer in the first edition that a rewrite could get clear right away from being included in plain terms at the start.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T11:36:14-08:00","id":1367821,"title":"","content":"I don't know if that interpretation helps resolve either the confusion or the underlying problem? <br /> <br /> But I don't have enough of a dog in this fight to argue further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-14-2020, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T12:05:02-08:00","id":1367826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367821#post1367821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure resolving the confusion between &quot;I'm doing this for the greater good!&quot; / &quot;I'm doing this for your own good!&quot; / &quot;I'm doing this for my own good!&quot; help resolve the underlying problem? Why include it at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters, it gets people to stop making infuriating mischaracterizations like &quot;Beasts think they're doing the right thing by inflicting cruelty upon the people around them,&quot; but also it gives them an actual direction besides &quot;Your Satiety's getting low, do you want to top it off in one major go or budge it up a little bit every day for a week? (Who you're getting it from is basically irrelevant.)&quot; That bit's important because the culture of lessons offers something resembling an explicit directive framework in a game where a lot of the story complications are player-pursuit-generated.<br /> <br /> The Begotten have an impact on their communities, and the nature of their feeding makes abstaining from community a non-option. Feeding in ways that progress or fulfill their Aspirations is more likely to be filling. Feeding in ways that involves their Lair or drains their Satiety is more likely to be filling. Accompanying other monsters in their processes of hunting and/or feeding is filling without risk of overfilling, particularly when Family Ties come into play.<br /> <br /> The dichotomy of the Satiety scale is &quot;you're more susceptible to supernatural mental influence, but you're a booster for other monsters, you're subtler, and your own supernatural mental influence works better&quot; and &quot;you're stronger on your own turf, but you're a more obvious threat and you're more likely to drive away any help you've got that isn't resigned to being with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The pieces exist for a Begotten character to be a primary or secondary driver in the local supernatural scene as it relates to mortals and monsters, and lessons narrow the scope a bit for a player who doesn't know what that means \u2014 &quot;What lessons are you trying to teach?&quot; is a framework of Aesop's Fables by way of gang activity and organized crime with a side of psychic landscaping.<br /> <br /> &quot;What lessons are you trying to teach?&quot; unfolds into &quot;What are the Aspirations you're trying to feed through your Hunger?&quot; &quot;How are you trying to get specific mortals/monsters/groups thereof to behave?&quot; &quot;What imagery and activity are you hitching your reputation to?&quot; and a bunch of other questions that inform the actions of a Beast, brood, or hive more thematically than &quot;You're hungry. How do you feed and on whom?&quot;<br /> <br /> You're a storyteller because you're attached to an ongoing story. You can try and make it mean something or it can be one more hungry shape in the dark corners of the world, but people are going to take something from it regardless, because it's in their heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:50:52-08:00","id":1367853,"title":"","content":"I haven't cracked open my copy of Beast in years, so I'll defer on how to characterize the &quot;lesson/teaching&quot; thing. I will say that in a game where the protagonists are by necessity abusive to less powerful people, using that language as a framework that guides their behavior has some adverse consequences to how sympathetic those protagonists can be because of real-world connotations and context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:52:40-08:00","id":1367854,"title":"","content":"Does Beast need a rewrite? Yes.<br /> <br /> Is there a chance of it happening any time soon? Not really, even with active OPP freelancers that want to do it, it's doesn't seem to be high on OPP's priority list compared to all the other books in te works.<br /> <br /> Is it going to make Beast into a different game? Nope. I'd love to sell more people on Beast, and I wish there wasn't a constant stream of Internet third hand stuff going around scaring people away from the game. It has some warts, but it's a strong game. But all of the complaints that amount to &quot;Beast needs to be a completely different game,&quot; aren't going to get what those people want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:16:17-08:00","id":1367862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367853#post1367853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that in a game where the protagonists are by necessity abusive to less powerful people</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Abusive&quot; is one of those hot-button words that only serves to obscure the actual extent of the harm necessarily being done.<br /> <br /> The Begotten can feed by stuff as petty as <i>a person realizing their watch has been stolen</i> or <i>a person seeing a broken window</i> or <i>a person nearly getting hit by a car after they jaywalked </i>or <i>a person realizing the cab they just took dropped them off in a bad part of town</i>. They gain sustenance from shocks of fear; the inclination of their Horror to go to known sources of sustenance when it wanders during extended lean times and the fact that more personally monstrous Beasts better manage to keep their relationships through abusive tactics does not make the whole &quot;species&quot; abusers by default in any sense where the term is useful to the discussion.<br /> <br /> By default, a Beast is powerful in the sense that it has supernatural powers. As a monster that can easily gain and leverage fame and notoriety, they is in a sense also capable of preying on people with less social power than them, but feeding that entails extended preparations and greater difficulty is another one of those things that makes a meal more likely to be filling and people in power tend to have more things to feed on, whether it be stuff or secrets or standing.<br /> <br /> By default, the needs of the Beastly constitution make you necessarily a nexus of nightmares and/or <i>kind of a shitty person,</i> and not even the kind particularly out of place among drug-peddling vampires, gristly trophy-displaying werewolf gangs, changelings running protection rackets, power-hungry mages, etc. A rewrite could stand to make that clear, but that's <i>already how it works now</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:08:20-08:00","id":1367886,"title":"","content":"This is why we generally direct people to the Player's Guide it does a pretty good job of being your clarificational rewrite for people. Like there's an entire section on Lessons just because people seem so keen to ignore everything else and argue that the Core says &quot;It's alright to be the most horrible abuser because you've decided its for their own good.&quot; Which is weird since the other easy interpretation of lessons in the core was &quot;Well if the Horror is going to try and feed regardless of my input- and I need to do it to live- I might as well try to do some good , or at least minimize damage, in the activity.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:27:36-08:00","id":1367891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367862#post1367862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default, the needs of the Beastly constitution make you necessarily a nexus of nightmares and/or <i>kind of a shitty person,</i> and not even the kind particularly out of place among drug-peddling vampires, gristly trophy-displaying werewolf gangs, changelings running protection rackets, power-hungry mages, etc. A rewrite could stand to make that clear, but that's <i>already how it works now</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but that's kind of a related problem, isn't it? You can Feed as a Beast with some trivial, petty stuff, right? You don't have to go on full abuser. But that kind of reduces the horror premise of the game to absurdity, doesn't it? &quot;I am the Primordial Serpent Lamia!&quot; cries the Beast. &quot;And I make people think they may have left their phone behind at the restaurant!&quot;<br /> <br /> Which goes to the basic problem. In order for Beasts to be scary, they have to be monsters, and in order to be monsters that feed off of fear, they have to abuse people. Take the example of a Tyrant who is the middle manager at a retail store, who feeds off making people fear being fired. That guy <i>exists</i>. The real world is full of petty tyrants like that. No one has ever been bitten by a vampire and no one ever will. There's an overlap between the feeding techniques that actually feel scary enough not to reduce the game to absurdity and real world abusive practices. If it's not a trivial fear, it's emotional abuse, and if it's a trivial fear, we're in a horror comedy. I do not know how to resolve this issue other than to go at it directly with no dissembling or drop it entirely.<br /> <br /> The other route is to keep it to exaggerated horror-movie level where the abusive practice is heavily attenuated by the familiar tropes of the horror genre; you have to drag someone into your lair once a year and chase them around as a giant spider until they pass out. Drop 'em off at home and hopefully they think it was a dream. That sort of stuff. And if you <i>don't </i>do it, you'll give everyone in town horrible nightmares when your Horror gets loose into the local subconscious.<br /> <br /> But what I can't see the game being able to manage is this weird half-step, where the Beast is just kind of an asshole. Does &quot;I am a primordial monster who feeds off the primal fears of mankind&quot; really feel like it's &quot;kind of an asshole&quot; territory? It'd be like Vampire but you had the option of shitposting on Twitter instead of drinking blood.<br /> <br /> But, again, I think the skeleton of the game is fine. It just needs the kind of refinement a good second edition brings to flesh it out some more. These sorts of conceptual issues are solvable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-14-2020, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T15:59:28-08:00","id":1367900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367891#post1367891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay but that's kind of a related problem, isn't it? You can Feed as a Beast with some trivial, petty stuff, right? You don't have to go on full abuser. But that kind of reduces the horror premise of the game to absurdity, doesn't it? &quot;I am the Primordial Serpent Lamia!&quot; cries the Beast. &quot;And I make people think they may have left their phone behind at the restaurant!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast <i>doesn't</i> cry that unless they're being absurd, is the thing. It's a <i>metaphorical</i> Primordial Serpent that feeds on the fear that someone has taken something of yours (and, unless you're leaning hard into the lowered signal-to-noise ratio of the modern Dream, its favorite food is probably not Missing Smartphone). In your Lair it's a very literal atavistic snake-monster, but the Astral is a realm of literalized abstractions.<br /> <br /> Outside of the Dream, the Primordial Serpent is <i>iconography.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what I can't see the game being able to manage is this weird half-step, where the Beast is just kind of an asshole. Does &quot;I am a primordial monster who feeds off the primal fears of mankind&quot; really feel like it's &quot;kind of an asshole&quot; territory? </div> </div> </div>Vlad III Dracula, Son of the Dragon, was infamous for his terror tactic of impaling people. He was far from the only ruler or noble whose heraldry included dragons, and the fact that he is as well-known as he is would translate directly to power in the Temenos.<br /> <br /> Vlad the Impaler is an outstanding example of the kind of notoriety that you work toward to become Incarnate. Most Beasts are not Vlad the Impaler (although many of them would probably like to be), much as most werewolves are not the Beast of Gevaudan and most changelings are not Queen Mab.<br /> <br /> This is why I keep coming back to the idea that the Kickstarter draft's writing was skewed too much in the direction of Low-Satiety-High-Lair Begotten \u2014 at the start, a Beast who is not in dire straits manages their meager Hunger by taking small bites and not rocking the boat too hard while they steer the resonance of their locale in such a fashion as is conducive to building their Legend and the Lair that houses it. Turning into a dragon is a climax point, not a constant.<br /> <br /> The part of Beast's premise that is &quot;Astral shamanoid&quot; deals with the fact that symbols and the collective unconscious are messy things with a lot of power in them, but going into the line craning your neck for Big Monster Setpieces to take priority over petty day-to-day villainy is going to skew expectations in a way that, yes, a rewrite needs to correct for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:06:10-08:00","id":1367904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367891#post1367891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay but that's kind of a related problem, isn't it? You can Feed as a Beast with some trivial, petty stuff, right? You don't have to go on full abuser. But that kind of reduces the horror premise of the game to absurdity, doesn't it? &quot;I am the Primordial Serpent Lamia!&quot; cries the Beast. &quot;And I make people think they may have left their phone behind at the restaurant!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I will never not enjoy how glorious those moments of being able to drop into the absurd are. Do know one of the Nightmares a Beast has literally is the fear of &quot;Crap this project is due tomorrow!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367891#post1367891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which goes to the basic problem. In order for Beasts to be scary, they have to be monsters, and in order to be monsters that feed off of fear, they have to abuse people. Take the example of a Tyrant who is the middle manager at a retail store, who feeds off making people fear being fired. That guy <i>exists</i>. The real world is full of petty tyrants like that. No one has ever been bitten by a vampire and no one ever will. There's an overlap between the feeding techniques that actually feel scary enough not to reduce the game to absurdity and real world abusive practices. If it's not a trivial fear, it's emotional abuse, and if it's a trivial fear, we're in a horror comedy. I do not know how to resolve this issue other than to go at it directly with no dissembling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can just do your job. Tyrant health inspector/ auditor if there is anything wrong they will find it and there is nothing you can do to stop them from marking you down for it or whatever is deemed appropriate by regulation. Hell the Core has a Namtaru nurse who just works in hospice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367891#post1367891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other route is to keep it to exaggerated horror-movie level where the abusive practice is heavily attenuated by the familiar tropes of the horror genre; you have to drag someone into your lair once a year and chase them around as a giant spider until they pass out. Drop 'em off at home and hopefully they think it was a dream. That sort of stuff. And if you <i>don't </i>do it, you'll give everyone in town horrible nightmares when your Horror gets loose into the local subconscious.<br /> <br /> But what I can't see the game being able to manage is this weird half-step, where the Beast is just kind of an asshole. Does &quot;I am a primordial monster who feeds off the primal fears of mankind&quot; really feel like it's &quot;kind of an asshole&quot; territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you just hang out with people who's feeding habits are less abhorrent to you. Hell even still horror to it, hang out with a Promethean feed when they get their stuff and all the while you're keeping an eye out as the disquiet builds. Are you and your friend going to be able to finish whatever you need and get out before it goes to shit. Are you going to be able to protect them and yourself if everything goes bad, how far are you willing to go to avoid that situation or protect your little family if you can't avoid the situation, is it even worth it to try?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:13:07-08:00","id":1367906,"title":"","content":"Does Beast need a rewrite? Yes.<br /> <br /> Does this thread's original post and subsequent advocates capture the knife's edge direction that Beast needs to walk and play on that will be fun, cathartic, meaningfully artistic, and tasteful in a way that will be attractive to a wider group while still being true to the spirit of the game that has earned it it's current fanbase?<br /> <br /> No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T16:48:06-08:00","id":1367921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367891#post1367891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay but that's kind of a related problem, isn't it? You can Feed as a Beast with some trivial, petty stuff, right? You don't have to go on full abuser. But that kind of reduces the horror premise of the game to absurdity, doesn't it? &quot;I am the Primordial Serpent Lamia!&quot; cries the Beast. &quot;And I make people think they may have left their phone behind at the restaurant!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to the response to this:<br /> <br /> The game has, you know, multiple parts to it that work together and mix around.<br /> <br /> Beasts that try to get by with these smaller petty feedings are also Beasts that have low Satiety because those are meager meals for their Horror. This creates a very different horror: they're one bad day from running out of Satiety and turning into the ravenous unstoppable monster they're trying to avoid becoming. If they screw up at all, their Horror will go running around feeding horribly in people's dreams, while the Beast will have to get it back into control be offering it up a tasty (aka super horrific to the victims) meal.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety Beasts get to have &quot;lighter&quot; meals, but they're on a razor's edge of losing their shit and tearing everything apart. Worse their Atavisms (which are generally brute force and dangerous powers) are at their strongest, while their Nightmares (their cerebral powers) are a their weakest, making it harder to walk that line.<br /> <br /> It's easy to pick a part of the game out and make it look absurd, but things need to be looked at in context. If you ignore all the downsides of Harmony 10, Werewolf would seem absurd that werewolves can just sin towards the Flesh until they can basically live as humans without any problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one has ever been bitten by a vampire and no one ever will. </div> </div> </div>Well nobody's ever been bitten by a supernatural vampire. Just like nobody's ever been a fear source for a Beast.<br /> <br /> Yes, Beast hits closer to home than some of the other games in this sense of having very human evils done by the monsters you play in it. Nobody here defending the game-as-is is going to deny that it might be too &quot;real&quot; for everyone to enjoy. That's fine, not every game is going to be for everyone. There's just a difference between, &quot;this game goes places I don't want to in a game,&quot; and, &quot;this game needs to be changed to suit my tastes.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does &quot;I am a primordial monster who feeds off the primal fears of mankind&quot; really feel like it's &quot;kind of an asshole&quot; territory? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd be like Vampire but you had the option of shitposting on Twitter instead of drinking blood. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's more like Changeling, but you can't passively feed off of people's emotions and have to force emotions on them.<br /> <br /> Because for all the talk of fear, it's the force that's the core issue that people generally have. Changeling would be a far more controversial game if harvesting glamour required you to manipulate people into feeling the emotions you're feeding from instead of being able to hang around highly emotional people and soak it in. Forcing people to feel love against their will gets really creepy really fast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T17:25:37-08:00","id":1367931,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I think the game needs to change all that much. Like I said, the skeleton is sound. If you wanted to come up with a &quot;general mythic monster catch-all&quot; game in the WoD-style framework you'd hit most of the same bullet points as Beast.<br /> <br /> But I do think the game is conceptually kind of complex and doesn't communicate itself well and since it deals with dark subject matter that resonates personally, it suffers for that lack of clarity more than, say, a game about being secret elves on a space station who use the power of rock &amp; roll to fight ghosts would suffer.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though to be fair, I levy that same criticism at basically the entire CofD these days. Jargon heavy, obscurantist writing, an almost total disregard for mechanical consistency or concision, etc. People seem to dig it anyway. Maybe I should finally realize I haven't enjoyed a WoD book in years and just bow out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-14-2020, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T17:26:19-08:00","id":1367932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot#post1367740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the actual game with Hunger and the horrifying abusive shit that must be done to satiate it just sucks every last bit of fun and goodwill out of it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman would be an entirely viable character concept for Beast: The Primordial. As a Beast, not a Hero. Just from the stuff the character does in comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T18:04:45-08:00","id":1367939,"title":"","content":"Beyond that, pretty much any vigilante/criminal hero/protagonist would work as a Beast on some level.<br /> <br /> The second your character can get away with breaking the law, and are still the &quot;good guy,&quot; they can probably be a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T00:16:27-08:00","id":1368474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367932#post1367932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman would be an entirely viable character concept for Beast: The Primordial. As a Beast, not a Hero. Just from the stuff the character does in comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>...hurm.<br /> <br /> *off to go thought experiment Phoenix-Joker as a Hero*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T12:39:24-08:00","id":1368785,"title":"","content":"really, if there was one thing I'd want a re-write for, it's how the Horror fits into the actions of a Beast. how is the legend of the Horror coming into play as the collective human unconcious starts to make sense of it. like the Corporate Ravager from Conquering Heroes, how does the Horror fit? <br /> <br /> Beast: the Primordial should talk about about the astral and how these legends start to take form. right now, it seems only the Beast is really in the minds of people, with the Horror only being vaguely mentioned. also, more on Lairs and just how odd they can be (and while a small part, an example of how dream logic works would be cool. a Hero and beast fighting in a lair, especially the Heart, should be plausibly told in an epic fashion, due to dream logic of course. the Anakim and Hero arent merely locked in a brawl, it's a desperate trek as the Hero traverses a mountainous maze, narrowly avoiding a yeti that just smashes the obstacles in his way...and the hero starts to notice a soft belly underneath all that fur)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T16:25:03-08:00","id":1368817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1368785#post1368785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">really, if there was one thing I'd want a re-write for, it's how the Horror fits into the actions of a Beast. how is the legend of the Horror coming into play as the collective human unconcious starts to make sense of it. like the Corporate Ravager from Conquering Heroes, how does the Horror fit?<br /> <br /> Beast: the Primordial should talk about about the astral and how these legends start to take form. right now, it seems only the Beast is really in the minds of people, with the Horror only being vaguely mentioned. also, more on Lairs and just how odd they can be (and while a small part, an example of how dream logic works would be cool. a Hero and beast fighting in a lair, especially the Heart, should be plausibly told in an epic fashion, due to dream logic of course. the Anakim and Hero arent merely locked in a brawl, it's a desperate trek as the Hero traverses a mountainous maze, narrowly avoiding a yeti that just smashes the obstacles in his way...and the hero starts to notice a soft belly underneath all that fur)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do you feel that the Player's Guide fails to go into these topics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T17:26:58-08:00","id":1368824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1368817#post1368817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How do you feel that the Player's Guide fails to go into these topics?</div> </div> </div> </div>huh? I assume this thread is like making a Beast 1.5 edition. the players guide is fine to me when talking about how these relate to the personal connections a Beast and horror has. even then though, the players guide does not really delve into the making of a Legend in terms of &quot;here's an example of how the Horror takes hold of the collective unconscious&quot;.<br /> <br /> hmm, perhaps the storyteller guide would be better suited to the latter parts of what I want to explained. also, I think Life and Legend has a chance at being a big part of the Beast. one part I liked about the players guide was describing how a particular beast's Legend and life will effect how they are viewed by a community, and how their Life affecting their legend can make it harder for a Hero to persecute them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T10:02:37-08:00","id":1369147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367932#post1367932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman would be an entirely viable character concept for Beast: The Primordial. As a Beast, not a Hero. Just from the stuff the character does in comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman doesn't usually take criminals to the Batcave and terrorize them to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T10:23:01-08:00","id":1369152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369147#post1369147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman doesn't usually take criminals to the Batcave and terrorize them to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts don't need to do that either. There are no rules in the book that force you to do something like that.<br /> <br /> So, you can still play a Beast like Batman, using the rules as written (and intended, I believe) with no issues, with little deviation from what Batman does in the comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:12:26-08:00","id":1369173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369147#post1369147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Batman doesn't usually take criminals to the Batcave and terrorize them to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, just like a lot of vigilante beasts, batman beats the ever loving shit out of them without killing them. in fact, beast dont even need to cause physical harm, just psychological damage (which batman also does)<br /> <br /> not that I'm against batman, he is pretty badass","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:43:01-08:00","id":1369178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369173#post1369173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> actually, just like a lot of vigilante beasts, batman beats the ever loving shit out of them without killing them. in fact, beast dont even need to cause physical harm, just psychological damage (which batman also does)<br /> <br /> not that I'm against batman, he is pretty badass</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are interpretations of Batman doing what he does as not being... well, they're not really healthy actions. There are ways to view Batman as being pretty monstrous, really. What makes his behavior more acceptable to our palates is that we feel those actions are directed at &quot;deserving&quot; or &quot;rightful&quot; targets. Put Batman's actions into the context of dealing with minority communities and.... things start getting a bit hinky there, ya know?<br /> <br /> A Beast with a Hunger for Punishment, a Nemesis, can fit very well into the shape that Batman provides. It can fit very well with the context of Beasts wanting to focus their feeding into providing Lessons. And a Beast might feel better about themselves as directing their feeding towards &quot;acceptable&quot; targets.<br /> <br /> What Batman does is still assaulting people. Still beating the crap out of people. Still terrorizing people. I think this is an interesting story to explore (and am actually doing so with a player, who picked a Hunger for Punishment for their Beast and are turning their attention towards gangs and criminals in the city he's in, so I've been giving a lot of thought about this). And these actions are still pretty monstrous. When you consider the acceptability of applying monstrous actions towards &quot;acceptable&quot; targets... Saying, &quot;This person deserves it, because I think they're doing something bad&quot; or &quot;That guys an asshole, so screw what happens to him&quot;.... These are slippery positions to take. <br /> <br /> There is an interesting darkness to explore regarding this particular topic, and that's why I think Batman makes for a very useful inspirational tool for a Beast concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:43:01-08:00","id":1369179,"title":"","content":"Edit: Didn't mean to double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:52:24-08:00","id":1369181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369179#post1369179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Didn't mean to double post.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as they're decent, interesting posts (as these were) double-posting is fine as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> I know that when I got it I was kind of put off by the Hunger stuff and what it ended up implying (the world need you, the Beast, to abuse other people to &quot;teach them lessons&quot;). Still, some of that might have come from additional (online) comments from others. So, I'm going to crack open the actual book (and the Player's Guide) to take a second look at the source material and see if that changes my impression of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:56:58-08:00","id":1369183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369181#post1369181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as they're decent, interesting posts (as these were) double-posting is fine as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> I know that when I got it I was kind of put off by the Hunger stuff and what it ended up implying (the world need you, the Beast, to abuse other people to &quot;teach them lessons&quot;). Still, some of that might have come from additional (online) comments from others. So, I'm going to crack open the actual book (and the Player's Guide) to take a second look at the source material and see if that changes my impression of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you prefer to take your own pace on this? Or would you appreciate your attention directed to certain areas of the book to be mindful of?<br /> <br /> If there is one thing I will fault the book for, is that some important contextual information is spread out a bit. Or at least, what I feel is important contextual information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T12:58:42-08:00","id":1369184,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2318\" data-vbnamecard=\"2318\">johntfs</a> I agree with you overall. I don\u2019t like Beast. I would never play one, and I would probably only allow them as NPCs if I ran a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:44:48-08:00","id":1369220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369173#post1369173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, just like a lot of vigilante beasts, batman beats the ever loving shit out of them without killing them. in fact, beast dont even need to cause physical harm, just psychological damage (which batman also does)<br /> <br /> not that I'm against batman, he is pretty badass</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Batman is that he's part of the superhero genre. His actions are acceptable for the reader because the reader has different expectations for what's acceptable or not, and the medium is slanted to make what he does seem like the right thing (except when it's trying to be subversive). Imagine instead someone who acts like Batman IRL. Vigilantism, intimidation, false imprisonment, aggravated assault, and even involuntary manslaughter at times. Someone who does all that is someone I want locked up, no matter how much I enjoy seeing Batman punch someone in the face.<br /> <br /> The question is then, is it acceptable to act like Batman in the Beast: The Primordial? The CofD setting is certainly not real life and there are just as fantastical beings in CofD as there is in the DC setting, but there's also a very, very different tone and different themes to CofD on a whole. Monsters are often sympathetic (one of the points in Hunter is that the hunters can sometimes be worse than the monsters) but they're most often monstrous, dangerous and destructive to any humans who come close even if they do have good intentions. In that regard Batman would fit right in, but in the context of CofD his actions would paint him as a well intentioned and tragic monster, not as a hero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369173#post1369173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in fact, beast dont even need to cause physical harm, just psychological damage (which batman also does)</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychological traumas can be just as bad and even worse than physical traumas. It's often just glossed over and ignored in superhero stories (and other genres) because it's difficult to portray in any meaningful way when it's not the focus of a story. While not an accurate depiction, CofD <i>doesn't</i> ignore the dangers of psychological damage, because it leads to negative Conditions and Integrity loss which makes the victim less resilient to further trauma. The victims can rebuild themselves, but they literally have to rebuild themselves to do so. Compare with physical damage, which heals quite easy and without any long term drawbacks as long as it's not aggravated damage (though at the point someone starts taking aggravated damage their chances for survival is starting to tank).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T15:51:41-08:00","id":1369223,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker is a book that has some important things to say about having violence in your games. I think it is very relevant to check out for better understanding of monstrous actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:28:36-08:00","id":1369237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367906#post1367906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Beast need a rewrite? Yes.<br /> <br /> Does this thread's original post and subsequent advocates capture the knife's edge direction that Beast needs to walk and play on that will be fun, cathartic, meaningfully artistic, and tasteful in a way that will be attractive to a wider group while still being true to the spirit of the game that has earned it it's current fanbase?<br /> <br /> No.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like the game before the Kickstarter revisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:43:49-08:00","id":1369242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369220#post1369220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is then, is it acceptable to act like Batman in the Beast: The Primordial?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what &quot;acceptable&quot; has to do with the question at hand.<br /> <br /> Acting like Batman is a perfectly functional way to act in Beast. It's whether or not people want to explore the fact that in Beast, Batman isn't a hero, because he's a monster, even if he's fighting to do more good than harm with his actions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:47:48-08:00","id":1369243,"title":"","content":"I personally think Beast would work better as a CtL antagonist supplement. Have Beasts be the Thallain to the Lost's Kithain. Probably created by Inferno/Abyss-corrupted True Fae or something of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T17:56:19-08:00","id":1369248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369243#post1369243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think Beast would work better as a CtL antagonist supplement. Have Beasts be the Thallain to the Lost's Kithain. Probably created by Inferno/Abyss-corrupted True Fae or something of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesus Inferno tainted True Fae... How would it play out,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T18:06:16-08:00","id":1369254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369243#post1369243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think Beast would work better as a CtL antagonist supplement. Have Beasts be the Thallain to the Lost's Kithain.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant\">I can't say I'm surprised.</a> Also, here as there, you're conflating Lost and Dreaming despite the two being different games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably created by Inferno/Abyss-corrupted True Fae or something of the sort. </div> </div> </div>That's not how any of that works.<br /> <br /> Putting aside the specifics of why, Inferno explicitly calls out the True Fae as not being subject to Infernal corruption, and the fae perspective on the Aeon of the Abyss is Tanglewoman/the Fourth Sister, whose entire deal is specifically antithetical to how the Fae do things.<br /> <br /> The Horrors of the Begotten are primordial things of fear, pain, and hunger, dressed up in human legend and folklore; that is consistent with Mage's long-extant descriptions of how the Anima Mundi and the Temenos operate, as could be expected from that being where they're from.<br /> <br /> &quot;The stuff that wants to break down the world and eat it&quot; and &quot;The stuff that can't be part of the world and therefore breaks it down&quot; does not have a monopoly on destructive behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T18:07:22-08:00","id":1369255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369248#post1369248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yesus Inferno tainted True Fae... How would it play out,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like normal True Fae, only intentionally evil and sadistic instead of obliviously so. See: Fomorians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T21:06:42-08:00","id":1369274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369237#post1369237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I quite like the game before the Kickstarter revisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to. I do not anymore. There are Very Noticeable Mistakes Made with it. I have commented on this before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369255#post1369255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like normal True Fae, only intentionally evil and sadistic instead of obliviously so. See: Fomorians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a lot of the other ideas for how to understand Beast as presented in this thread, I find this <i>painfully</i> short-sighted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-20T23:23:25-08:00","id":1369283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369254#post1369254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1338018-does-anyone-else-feel-changelings-make-most-of-beast-the-primordial-seem-redundant\">I can't say I'm surprised.</a> Also, here as there, you're conflating Lost and Dreaming despite the two being different games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I'm not conflating them, don't be deliberately obtuse. I'm merely using the Thallain <i>as an example </i>of what sort of role I think Beast could potentially fulfIll in CtL, and CofD as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369254#post1369254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how any of that works.<br /> <br /> Putting aside the specifics of why, Inferno explicitly calls out the True Fae as not being subject to Infernal corruption, and the fae perspective on the Aeon of the Abyss is Tanglewoman/the Fourth Sister, whose entire deal is specifically antithetical to how the Fae do things.<br /> <br /> The Horrors of the Begotten are primordial things of fear, pain, and hunger, dressed up in human legend and folklore; that is consistent with Mage's long-extant descriptions of how the Anima Mundi and the Temenos operate, as could be expected from that being where they're from.<br /> <br /> &quot;The stuff that wants to break down the world and eat it&quot; and &quot;The stuff that can't be part of the world and therefore breaks it down&quot; does not have a monopoly on destructive behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. And it's why I said corrupted by the Abyss/Inferno instead of allied with or hailing from them. The idea being they were originally beings of a different nature that got tainted and twisted by eldritch, otherwordly forces into things-not-meant-to-be. See, the Su'ur from WtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T05:19:29-08:00","id":1369334,"title":"","content":"Its important to not overstate beastly feeding as uniquely horrible. Their feeding explicitly needn't be breaking point level: any assertion of power can feed a tyrant, for example. I don't find beasts doing anything out of line with vampires, prometheans, or hunters, either in my actual experience or in the books. People can even explicitly be willing; and I've had PCs volunteer themselves for such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1367891#post1367891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that kind of reduces the horror premise of the game to absurdity, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're supposed to enjoy the feeding in Beast. If you don't feed, the worst you will do is give people bad dreams. While bad dreams are bad, they're also something the protagonist had to deal with his whole life. I wouldn't worry too much about any expectation that a beast's feedings have to be a certain level of bad.<br /> <br /> Also if they made a new version of Beast, probably a thinly veiled 3rd edition version (a la Blood &amp; Smoke: the Strix Chronicles, before they got the greenlight for a new edition), I'd buy it because I love Beast. If they made an actual 3rd edition of CofD in general right after all these KSes for 2e stuff, though, I don't think that'd work well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 02-21-2020, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T11:39:42-08:00","id":1369412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369242#post1369242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what &quot;acceptable&quot; has to do with the question at hand.<br /> <br /> Acting like Batman is a perfectly functional way to act in Beast. It's whether or not people want to explore the fact that in Beast, Batman isn't a hero, because he's a monster, even if he's fighting to do more good than harm with his actions.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, one thing that kind of hit when I looked at the types of Hungers was, &quot;You know who else would have made a really good Beast? Osama bin Laden.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> High Satiety: For high Satiety, the destruction must be<br /> obvious and extensive, or the target must be widely accepted to<br /> be valuable or in use by many people. A Beast could destroy a<br /> large swath of property and then feast on the feelings of horror<br /> as the pictures go viral. She could kill a beloved celebrity, or<br /> smash a religious artifact. </div> </div> </div>It's interesting that none of of the Satiety condition are wholly good. At Gorged the Beast isn't as resistant to other supernatural mental effects. At Slumbering, he's basically a human. If it weren't for Heroes (and the horrific cost of getting to Satiety 10), that's almost a good endpoint for a Beast. The Horror has gone beddie-bye and now the dude doesn't have to do horrible shit to people.<br /> Even the middle ground of Sated allow Heroes to put Anathema on Beasts. Meanwhile Starves screws with your ability to do anything other than trying to feed and Ravenous fucks with you even worse in that you pretty much <i>can't</i> do anything other than try to get fed. Oh, and getting fed means you either kill a Hero (good luck on that while you're out of juice) or do something along the line of the 9-11 attacks or killing John Lennon. At which point you get exactly 1 point of Satiety.<br /> <br /> A hungry Vampire can seriously hurt or even kill people in feeding if they lose control. Maybe take out four or five in a Frenzy. A Ravenous Beast ... well, One World Trade Center was great while it lasted...<br /> <br /> Back in the 80s there was a pretty big movement against &quot;bad media.&quot; Explicit music lyrics, violent/sexual movies, and, yes, role-playing games. Tom Hanks starred in <i>Mazes and Monsters</i> playing a guy who lost his shit playing not-D&amp;D. Later in the 90s or 00s some twit made a game called F.A.T.A.L. which seemed to be trying make all the horrible lies people told about D&amp;D real (there's a chart so you can determine the circumferences of someone's anus to see if your dick can fit in it without damaging them. The chart includes sizes for infants. And there was a bonus to size if the person is slutty. So... slutty babies you can assfuck).<br /> <br /> Most of the various &quot;monster&quot; books present those within as beings who might do awful things but who are in general just trying to get along and live their lives. And as such Hunters shouldn't be trying to exterminate them. Beasts seem almost purpose-built to justify the existence of Hunters.<br /> <br /> I'll keep reading and at least try to keep an open mind, but so far this game is not making a very good second first impression with me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T12:15:25-08:00","id":1369421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369412#post1369412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the various &quot;monster&quot; books present those within as beings who might do awful things but who are in general just trying to get along and live their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is patently false.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as such Hunters shouldn't be trying to exterminate them. </div> </div> </div>This is even more patently false, seeing as the latest occurrences of Hunter analogues as an antagonist type that I can remember pre-date Hunter as a gameline and all of those focus on the fact that there are mortals who will try to kill you for various reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts seem almost purpose-built to justify the existence of Hunters. </div> </div> </div>In the sense that they're hard to ignore by design, sure, but the things Beasts do to feed almost uniformly look like normal human activities with the occasional terrifying supernatural edge. Their activities justify the existence of hunters about as much as cults do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll keep reading and at least try to keep an open mind, but so far this game is not making a very good second first impression with me. </div> </div> </div>The fact that you jump to a terror attack that involved crashing airliners into a famous part of a major city's skyline or killing a world-famous musician as examples for the Big Meal category of the Hunger For Ruin suggests to me that you could stand to try a little harder.<br /> <br /> Set down your preconceptions and turn down the dials of your assumed readings of the text. These are monsters whose role was least complicated before the rise of media; they're local terrors whose impact has been expanded by advances in travel and communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T12:59:34-08:00","id":1369426,"title":"","content":"Replicating something like the 9/11 attack is ridiculously overkill for an example High Satiety event for Hunger for Ruin. In general, you shouldn't be focusing on such extremes for anything you do to feed your hungers. It's just not necessary and actually detrimental towards focusing the game on the local community. As a more reasonable example of a High Satiety Ruin feeding, I'd accept a Beast breaking the stained glass windows of the local prominent church. High profile for the community, attacks something that a lot of the people feel a strong connection to. It would certainly be the talk of the town and cause a reaction from people.<br /> <br /> Regarding Satiety Conditions... A factor that really impresses me with their design is how they really catch Beasts coming and going. None of them are really comfortable states to be in. Not even Slumbering.<br /> <br /> When you're Ravenous, you're out of control with your Hunger, having to take any minor opportunities you see even though they don't help you beyond giving you the will to keep pushing forward just a bit longer, while you're slowly starving to death.<br /> <br /> When you're Starving, you're constantly jonesing for your next fix. You're restless and on edge, encouraging you to be reckless with your behavior. This is sustainable, but an uncomfortable state to be in.<br /> <br /> When you're Sated... You're actually doing pretty decent. Unfortunately, while it's doable to reach this state, it's also rather dangerous for you, opening you up to Anathema from Heroes.<br /> <br /> When you're Gorged, you're now feeling lethargic. Not only are you more suggestible from supernatural effects, but you're more apt to fail tasks because it's just so difficult for you to keep yourself active and engaged with whats going on around you.<br /> <br /> When you're Slumbering... while you're now feeling functionally human... you're also contending with depression on top of losing all the kinds of advantages that help keep you safe from supernatural threats and Heroes.<br /> <br /> And this is pretty deliberate. A Beast looking to minimize the harm they do can try to stay around the Sated area, either focusing on doing many small feedings to bump from Starving back to Sated to balance themselves out, or doing more meaningful, more damaging feedings from a single target each time that lets you last longer between feedings, effectively balancing from Gorged and Sated.<br /> <br /> Now, there is another path to take, but one that requires being more active in the local supernatural community. Taking advantage of Family Dinner and participating in the hunts of other supernatural entities can be a useful way to extend how often your own feedings have to occur. This is also deliberate.<br /> <br /> ....I gotta admit though... I'm really puzzled as to how the monstrosity of the other splats keep getting downplayed whenever the monstrosity of Beasts gets discussed. Like vampires assaulting people for their blood isn't assault, like werewolves chasing and hunting someone down isn't a terrifying experience for them, like leeching off of other people's personal grief isn't an invasion of privacy or creepy as hell. My guess is that it's a factor of a feeling of separation through metaphor, but it's been a consideration in my mind that what these monsters do is always... well, monstrous. I think taking away the human aspects of the behavior that the monsters symbolize takes away from the visceral nature of the base acts.<br /> <br /> Part of what really fascinates me with the Chronicles of Darkness games is there is a real discussion going on about the nature of monstrosity and what can be done with it. Do you use your monstrous nature for your own purposes? Do you try to do some good with it? Do you limit your predation to feel like you're being moral with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:07:34-08:00","id":1369444,"title":"","content":"Adding to Paradim's excellent points, if you want to play a 'good' Beast? If you really, really want to be a net boon to your community? It's 100% possible. The easiest way is probably learning the Relentless Hunter Atavism and befriending a vampire or two. Helping the vampire track down and lightly feed from a mortal is as much as a 3 satiety to 1 lethal trade and if you're keeping them fed on your own nigh limitless blood supply the rest of the week you're drastically reducing that vampire's... eco footprint, as it were.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing; Beasts aren't well equipped to directly benefit humanity. At best they're probably in Batman territory, doing a certain amount of harm in the process of a hopefully greater amount of good. Where they do better is helping other monster communities. As in the Vampire example above there are multiple ways a Beast can keep mortals safe just by virtue of providing alternative resources for other monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:28:21-08:00","id":1369447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369444#post1369444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding to Paradim's excellent points, if you want to play a 'good' Beast? If you really, really want to be a net boon to your community? It's 100% possible. The easiest way is probably learning the Relentless Hunter Atavism and befriending a vampire or two. Helping the vampire track down and lightly feed from a mortal is as much as a 3 satiety to 1 lethal trade and if you're keeping them fed on your own nigh limitless blood supply the rest of the week you're drastically reducing that vampire's... eco footprint, as it were.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing; Beasts aren't well equipped to directly benefit humanity. At best they're probably in Batman territory, doing a certain amount of harm in the process of a hopefully greater amount of good. Where they do better is helping other monster communities. As in the Vampire example above there are multiple ways a Beast can keep mortals safe just by virtue of providing alternative resources for other monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've... some opinions on this... And I'm not really sure this is the place to get into them. I'll be pretty blunt in saying that thinking of delving into those opinions makes me a bit uncomfortable. <br /> <br /> I will say that I deeply value Beast: The Primordial for being a game that makes me pause, to stop and reflect on what characters are actively doing. It's a place that I actually feel pretty safe for diving into some darker emotions and for considering things that normally make me uncomfortable. That a game can provide this actually feels pretty liberating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T14:53:12-08:00","id":1369451,"title":"","content":"0 Satiety is a terrible place to be because you do need to go rather extreme to get out. Unless you hit 0 during the planing of a major feed you're probably not doing that since that requires a chapter and Ravenous deals 1 point of damage a day that can only be repaired by external mystical healing, so your not likely to get a base feeding of 5 is due to time constraints. (Though it does make things so much easier if you can) Ergo you'll want to go moderate as that's a base feed of 3 and as the time requirements are only a scene of prep/pursuit is more agreeable to ravenous Beghotten's timetable.<br /> <br /> Now the odds of someone dying when a Beghotten is at 0 and needs to feed are high, I mean its a +4 so in a desperate situation a Beast might not be as willing to turn down that chunk of food it represents. That said there are other methods for it. If your ST is willing to allow &quot;No longer be Ravenous&quot; as a short term aspiration then the Ravager burning down a beloved landmark (an medium tier feed, but doesn't require too much prep time and I will note the book discourages casualties as it limits the number of people affected by the act) counts as in pursuit of/ fulfilling an aspiration for an additional +2, maybe even +3. The target landmark was picked because it was well loved thus abundant feeding for an additional +3 for a comfortable 8 point meal. If you can't get the aspiration then you work in a method for making the feeding tie to your unique aspect of the hunger and maybe spread some Rubidrium around to make it burn purple for that added touch of strange to go for the unique feeding bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T15:01:19-08:00","id":1369453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369412#post1369412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, one thing that kind of hit when I looked at the types of Hungers was, &quot;You know who else would have made a really good Beast? Osama bin Laden.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Beasts need to feed once a week at a minimum (if using the real-time chart instead of going with the more narrative option, which doesn't really change much for the overall point). Someone that spends years hiding between mass casualty terrorist attacks would, as a Beast, end up at Satiety 0 or 10 in short order (either 0 from bleeding Satiety without regular meals, or 10 from such a devastating action). A Ravenous Beast is hardly capable of running an international terrorist organization to perpetuate more mass casualty attacks, especially with the taking 1 Lethal Damage every day part. A Slumbering Beast now doesn't have all those cool abilities to avoid people trying to kill them for all those murders their responsible for.<br /> <br /> Batman-as-Beast is functional because his methods ensure he has easy access to feeding at all levels of Satiety.<br /> <br /> Osama bin Laden-as-Beast isn't functional because it's too oriented around mass Satiety feeding events that take too much time between them.<br /> <br /> Even toning done the terrorist angle? Ted Kaczynski isn't a functional Beast either. Over 17 years he was responsible for 16 bombs, two of which failed. A Beast can't get by on 14 feedings over 17 years. The Unabomber (who only killed three people) might have shoved himself into at least the America cultural landscape, but he would have made for a very unsuccessful Beast.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at a vile mother fucker that's would manage to work as a Beast? John Leonard Orr, aka the Pillow Pyro, is a much better example. A serial arsonist suspected of setting over 2,000 fires over just seven years. Many quite small, but some (the ones the focused on convicting him for) quite major. One federal agent estimated that fires in his area dropped <b>90%</b> after this arrest. While lesser known to the wider public, he killed one more person and caused vastly more damage than Kaczynski did.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of these three individuals actually got an ending a Beast would be happy about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's interesting that none of of the Satiety condition are wholly good. </div> </div> </div>Yes, as well detailed by Paradim, this is wholly intentional and a huge positive towards playing the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile Starves screws with your ability to do anything other than trying to feed... </div> </div> </div>Um... not really? The massive -2 penalty to opening Primordial Pathways is hardly going to mess up your daily life much. The Beat point for it is pretty nasty, but that's up to the player on how often they want it to come up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and getting fed means you either kill a Hero (good luck on that while you're out of juice) or do something along the line of the 9-11 attacks or killing John Lennon. At which point you get exactly 1 point of Satiety. </div> </div> </div>Killing a Hero at Ravenous isn't has bad at is sounds. All of your Atavisms are still pumped up, and you can spend Willpower because it's in pursuit of Satiety.<br /> <br /> You're also skipping the very simple-if-risky option: the Horror just handles it. You roll a chance die once a day as your Horror goes to hunt for itself (this is automatic), and on a 10, you get 1 Satiety and move from Ravenous to Starving (and should low Satiety feed ASAP). Or you roll a 1 and Heroes come to you so you can kill one of them. While death is certainly a serious risk for a Ravenous Beast, the rules aren't so punishing that you might as well rip up your sheet the second you hit Satiety 0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back in the 80s there was a pretty big movement against &quot;bad media.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what the point of all this retelling of RPG history is.<br /> <br /> And you don't need to lecture people about FATAL, lots of us know about it.<br /> <br /> You seem more interested in an excuse to talk about raping children than actually talking about Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the various &quot;monster&quot; books present those within as beings who might do awful things but who are in general just trying to get along and live their lives. And as such Hunters shouldn't be trying to exterminate them. Beasts seem almost purpose-built to justify the existence of Hunters. </div> </div> </div>The same goes for Beasts. They're just trying to get along and live their lives. Not sating their Horrors is fatal.... so that's part of living for them. Most Hunter groups wish more monsters were like Beasts in a quiet different way: actually trying to do good for humanity instead of just being selfish pricks or serving some entity that doesn't exactly care about human life.<br /> <br /> But as also noted about the disconnect here is quite boggling. A vampire can kill a mortal every night, but vampires are &quot;OK&quot; monsters, while a Beast steals an expensive item once a week and they're morally the same as mass casualty terrorists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T16:41:48-08:00","id":1369472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369453#post1369453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as also noted about the disconnect here is quite boggling. A vampire can kill a mortal every night, but vampires are &quot;OK&quot; monsters, while a Beast steals an expensive item once a week and they're morally the same as mass casualty terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I'm gonna say it. People don't need to agree with me about this and I'm not throwing accusations around. (Heavy Arms, I'm using this comment as a springboard, and it's absolutely not specifically directed at you. It's not specifically directed at anyone!)<br /> <br /> I'm always starkly reminded in this talks about the awfulness of Beasts in particular, about how disparately treated minority groups are for similar offenses that majority demographics commit.<br /> <br /> Beast: The Primordial offers as recommended reading a non-fiction book titled &quot;On Monsters: An Unnatural History of Our Worst Fears&quot; by Stephen Asma. I bought this book because it seemed pretty relevant to the content, and I'm honestly very glad I did. The monsters we create always emphasize real fears that people have. I don't say &quot;real&quot; as in &quot;rightfully legitimate&quot;, I mean &quot;real&quot; as in &quot;people really do have these fears&quot;. A lot of the monsters we make are based upon the fear of the Other. I'm still processing this book.<br /> <br /> I strongly recommend this book, because it really helps you think about what monsters mean to us culturally. It's helped me to stop and consider things more deeply. To stop and listen more. And really, it's helped me to appreciate Beast: The Primordial a lot more for what it can offer.<br /> <br /> The monsters we create speaks volumes about us as people. Considering that has given me a lot to think about.<br /> <br /> I've picked up &quot;Monster Theory: Reading Cultures&quot;, edited by Jeffery Cohen as it is a collection of essays to check out next and I'm pretty excited about it! ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T16:51:28-08:00","id":1369473,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, regarding &quot;most hunter groups wish monsters were more like beast&quot;, I actually got from Tooth and Nail that most wish they were because beasts tend to not cause physical harm or make slaves out of humans compared to other monsters. most dont know about them wanting to teach lessons I think<br /> <br /> and yeah, the fact some beasts can literally feed by breaking some property is treated as infinitely worse worse than blood drinking vampires, werewolves that will kill you for unknowingly messing up the Shadow, and golems that make supernatural disasters just by existing is crazy.<br /> <br /> really, I would say beasts Building their Legends are as morally gray as mages chasing their Obsessions. which is to say, a healthy amount (damn though, all these complaints toward beast make me worry about how a 2nd edition kickstarter would go.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T19:01:04-08:00","id":1369483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369453#post1369453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. Beasts need to feed once a week at a minimum (if using the real-time chart instead of going with the more narrative option, which doesn't really change much for the overall point). Someone that spends years hiding between mass casualty terrorist attacks would, as a Beast, end up at Satiety 0 or 10 in short order (either 0 from bleeding Satiety without regular meals, or 10 from such a devastating action). A Ravenous Beast is hardly capable of running an international terrorist organization to perpetuate more mass casualty attacks, especially with the taking 1 Lethal Damage every day part. A Slumbering Beast now doesn't have all those cool abilities to avoid people trying to kill them for all those murders their responsible for.<br /> <br /> Batman-as-Beast is functional because his methods ensure he has easy access to feeding at all levels of Satiety.<br /> <br /> Osama bin Laden-as-Beast isn't functional because it's too oriented around mass Satiety feeding events that take too much time between them.<br /> <br /> Even toning done the terrorist angle? Ted Kaczynski isn't a functional Beast either. Over 17 years he was responsible for 16 bombs, two of which failed. A Beast can't get by on 14 feedings over 17 years. The Unabomber (who only killed three people) might have shoved himself into at least the America cultural landscape, but he would have made for a very unsuccessful Beast.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at a vile mother fucker that's would manage to work as a Beast? John Leonard Orr, aka the Pillow Pyro, is a much better example. A serial arsonist suspected of setting over 2,000 fires over just seven years. Many quite small, but some (the ones the focused on convicting him for) quite major. One federal agent estimated that fires in his area dropped <b>90%</b> after this arrest. While lesser known to the wider public, he killed one more person and caused vastly more damage than Kaczynski did.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of these three individuals actually got an ending a Beast would be happy about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, as well detailed by Paradim, this is wholly intentional and a huge positive towards playing the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Um... not really? The massive -2 penalty to opening Primordial Pathways is hardly going to mess up your daily life much. The Beat point for it is pretty nasty, but that's up to the player on how often they want it to come up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Killing a Hero at Ravenous isn't has bad at is sounds. All of your Atavisms are still pumped up, and you can spend Willpower because it's in pursuit of Satiety.<br /> <br /> You're also skipping the very simple-if-risky option: the Horror just handles it. You roll a chance die once a day as your Horror goes to hunt for itself (this is automatic), and on a 10, you get 1 Satiety and move from Ravenous to Starving (and should low Satiety feed ASAP). Or you roll a 1 and Heroes come to you so you can kill one of them. While death is certainly a serious risk for a Ravenous Beast, the rules aren't so punishing that you might as well rip up your sheet the second you hit Satiety 0.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea what the point of all this retelling of RPG history is.<br /> <br /> And you don't need to lecture people about FATAL, lots of us know about it.<br /> <br /> You seem more interested in an excuse to talk about raping children than actually talking about Beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The same goes for Beasts. They're just trying to get along and live their lives. Not sating their Horrors is fatal.... so that's part of living for them. Most Hunter groups wish more monsters were like Beasts in a quiet different way: actually trying to do good for humanity instead of just being selfish pricks or serving some entity that doesn't exactly care about human life.<br /> <br /> But as also noted about the disconnect here is quite boggling. A vampire can kill a mortal every night, but vampires are &quot;OK&quot; monsters, while a Beast steals an expensive item once a week and they're morally the same as mass casualty terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts feed by deliberately inflicting physical and psychological pain/terror/distress on others. If somebody gets fed on by a vampire, there's a decent chance they won't even really notice it. A bit weak/dizzy the next day? Maybe. They'll chalk it up to partying to hard and sleeping too little or something similar. The main aftereffects might be some weirdly erotic dreams about somebody wearing sunglasses after dark.<br /> <br /> Let's look again at the High/Medium/Low aspect of Satiety for Ruin:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Ravager hunts for annihilation. She aims to destroy<br /> that which others value, or at least take for granted. The<br /> connection to people determines how fulfilling the destruction<br /> is. Something one person cherishes is somewhat valuable, but<br /> something recognized by a large swath of the population as<br /> important is significantly more so. The Horror sates itself on<br /> the feeling of breaking the world, and on the tears of those who<br /> must watch that world crumble. The moment of shock comes<br /> when the target(s) see the destruction the Beast has wrought.<br /> <br /> High Satiety: For high Satiety, the destruction must be<br /> obvious and extensive, or the target must be widely accepted to<br /> be valuable or in use by many people. A Beast could destroy a<br /> large swath of property and then feast on the feelings of horror<br /> as the pictures go viral. She could kill a beloved celebrity, or<br /> smash a religious artifact.<br /> <br /> Moderate Satiety: The item destroyed must be extremely<br /> important to at least a small group of people. The Beast might<br /> burn down a church (doing so with the congregation inside<br /> is actually not preferable, because then not as many people<br /> mourn the loss of the church), kill a local character that the<br /> neighborhood knows and loves, or smash all the windows of<br /> all the cars in a particular garage.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: For low Satiety, if it bleeds, it works. If<br /> someone is hurt significantly in a way they\u2019ll remember for at<br /> least a week, it\u2019s enough. If the destruction is enough to (make?)<br /> a family cry \u2014 burn a car, kill a pet, cut down an old tree \u2014 the Horror<br /> can feed. The Beast doesn\u2019t have to remain anonymous, but<br /> doing so keeps the focus on the destruction, rather than the<br /> destructor (and, obviously, keeps the authorities off her tail). </div> </div> </div>Look at those potential feedings. They're all things that a real person could do in the real world. I can't stare into your eyes and make you do my will. Or turn into a nine-foot tall killing furry death beast. Or cause the gas main in your building to explode through my connection with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> But... burn your car? Cut down that tree your great-grandmother planted as a little girl? Kill your cute doggie? I could do that. Not would, but could. Those are tasks within my ability as a human being in the real world to accomplish. Even the other stuff is at least possible. Burn your church? Maybe. Kill the nice old lady that bakes cookies for the neighborhood kids? Perhaps. Smash a bunch of car windows? With effort.<br /> <br /> And for the High levels there's a reason we know the names Mark David Chapman and Osama bin Laden. They weren't supernatural monsters, just fucked up human beings, when they did the evil shit they did.<br /> <br /> I think that's the biggest &quot;fall down&quot; of Beast - and maybe it's greatest strength. If Mage uses Life magick to turn your into a frog then boils you and eats your frog legs, that's a pretty horrifying thing. But it's an unreal horrifying thing. Because that doesn't actually happen in the real world. But if somebody rapes your wife or kill your child to &quot;teach you a lesson,&quot; well, that shit happens in the real world. Jack the Ripper thought he was doing God's work going after prostitutes. There just seems to be some stuff in Beast that can be and has been used in the service of justifying really awful people doing really awful things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T19:28:47-08:00","id":1369488,"title":"","content":"Ruin has always struck me as the hardest Hunger to bend toward nobler goals. The best I've been able to come up with there is an arsonist who targets unsafe buildings when they're empty, a sort of pre-emptive &quot;Wow look at all these fire code violations, imagine if this had happened when people were home&quot; fuck you at landlords who ignore the safety of their tenants.<br /> <br /> But that's only one of five (and later seven). What about Low Satiety Prey, which can explicitly be sated by hunting deer and similar activities?<br /> <br /> Also, High Satiety feeding is generally going to be exceedingly rare. Unless you're actively pursuing the Slumbering condition or have fallen to Ravenous it's not just more trouble than it's worth to set up it's actively counter to the goal of staying fed but awake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","user":"HelmsDerp","date":". 02-21-2020, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T19:37:56-08:00","id":1369490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369483#post1369483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts feed by deliberately inflicting physical and psychological pain/terror/distress on others. If somebody gets fed on by a vampire, there's a decent chance they won't even really notice it. A bit weak/dizzy the next day? Maybe. They'll chalk it up to partying to hard and sleeping too little or something similar. The main aftereffects might be some weirdly erotic dreams about somebody wearing sunglasses after dark.<br /> <br /> Let's look again at the High/Medium/Low aspect of Satiety for Ruin:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Look at those potential feedings. They're all things that a real person could do in the real world. I can't stare into your eyes and make you do my will. Or turn into a nine-foot tall killing furry death beast. Or cause the gas main in your building to explode through my connection with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> But... burn your car? Cut down that tree your great-grandmother planted as a little girl? Kill your cute doggie? I could do that. Not would, but could. Those are tasks within my ability as a human being in the real world to accomplish. Even the other stuff is at least possible. Burn your church? Maybe. Kill the nice old lady that bakes cookies for the neighborhood kids? Perhaps. Smash a bunch of car windows? With effort.<br /> <br /> And for the High levels there's a reason we know the names Mark David Chapman and Osama bin Laden. They weren't supernatural monsters, just fucked up human beings, when they did the evil shit they did.<br /> <br /> I think that's the biggest &quot;fall down&quot; of Beast - and maybe it's greatest strength. If Mage uses Life magick to turn your into a frog then boils you and eats your frog legs, that's a pretty horrifying thing. But it's an unreal horrifying thing. Because that doesn't actually happen in the real world. But if somebody rapes your wife or kill your child to &quot;teach you a lesson,&quot; well, that shit happens in the real world. Jack the Ripper thought he was doing God's work going after prostitutes. There just seems to be some stuff in Beast that can be and has been used in the service of justifying really awful people doing really awful things.</div> </div> </div> </div>the Kiss is literally sexual in nature. a vampire can &quot;Kiss&quot; unwilling victims. theres a reason some players I know consider the kiss comparable to rape at times. it's also why there is an option to do feeding scenes without needing to roleplay it<br /> <br /> and again, you're claiming high satiety means &quot;Osama Bin Laden&quot; level mayhem. it does not, really doesnt and by repeating it, all you do is show a willing ignorance to what people like Heavy Arms, Paradim, and Satchel have said. high satiety Ruin can happen simply by taking apart a very strong bond between two people. it can even be done by taking down a criminal organization, a very good thing. I think you are funneling every action a Beast could through only extreme and negative acts. no one, and I think most beasts who try to teach lessons (not all do) dont RAPE people to teach.<br /> <br /> also, if we are to look at mages as real, i would consider being turned into a frog and eaten just as terrifying as a beast with a hunger for prey hunting me down<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd really suggest the players guide, I know you are already getting it I think, but you must realize that book is basically what beast should've been like (in terms of mood and tone) from the beginning, and it expands on their culture<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think another mindset issue you have is that many horrible things a monster does is somehow excusable because you yourself cant do it that way. that's kinda making it convenient to ignore beast can breath fire, flip cars with a hand, and all kinds of other things normal humans cant do in order to accomplish their goals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-21-2020, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T19:56:55-08:00","id":1369494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369483#post1369483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at those potential feedings. They're all things that a real person could do in the real world. I can't stare into your eyes and make you do my will. Or turn into a nine-foot tall killing furry death beast. Or cause the gas main in your building to explode through my connection with the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts can kinda do each of those things, actually....<br /> <br /> Using the Nightmare &quot;You Must Obey&quot; absolutely lets you stare into someone's eyes and make them do your will.<br /> <br /> Merging your Lair with the area definitely turns you into a horror movie monster.<br /> <br /> Now Beasts don't have a connection to the Supernal.... But causing the gas main to explode? Hell, use Dragonfire to set the whole building on fire! You can dance amongst the flames! Pretty much the same thing.<br /> <br /> Beasts are absolutely supernatural monsters.<br /> <br /> I'm still confused as to how a vampire feeding from someone unwilling isn't a terrible thing. Feeding for a vampire is like <i>sex </i>to them. Like... Think about that. To state it more clearly, vampires often get used as rape metaphors. Werewolf: The Forsaken at least does a little better of stepping away from origins of werewolves being domestic abuser metaphors...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T20:08:48-08:00","id":1369495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369483#post1369483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts feed by deliberately inflicting physical and psychological pain/terror/distress on others. If somebody gets fed on by a vampire, there's a decent chance they won't even really notice it. A bit weak/dizzy the next day? Maybe. They'll chalk it up to partying to hard and sleeping too little or something similar. The main aftereffects might be some weirdly erotic dreams about somebody wearing sunglasses after dark.<br /> <br /> Let's look again at the High/Medium/Low aspect of Satiety for Ruin:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Look at those potential feedings. They're all things that a real person could do in the real world. I can't stare into your eyes and make you do my will. Or turn into a nine-foot tall killing furry death beast. Or cause the gas main in your building to explode through my connection with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> But... burn your car? Cut down that tree your great-grandmother planted as a little girl? Kill your cute doggie? I could do that. Not would, but could. Those are tasks within my ability as a human being in the real world to accomplish. Even the other stuff is at least possible. Burn your church? Maybe. Kill the nice old lady that bakes cookies for the neighborhood kids? Perhaps. Smash a bunch of car windows? With effort.<br /> <br /> And for the High levels there's a reason we know the names Mark David Chapman and Osama bin Laden. They weren't supernatural monsters, just fucked up human beings, when they did the evil shit they did.<br /> <br /> I think that's the biggest &quot;fall down&quot; of Beast - and maybe it's greatest strength. If Mage uses Life magick to turn your into a frog then boils you and eats your frog legs, that's a pretty horrifying thing. But it's an unreal horrifying thing. Because that doesn't actually happen in the real world. But if somebody rapes your wife or kill your child to &quot;teach you a lesson,&quot; well, that shit happens in the real world. Jack the Ripper thought he was doing God's work going after prostitutes. There just seems to be some stuff in Beast that can be and has been used in the service of justifying really awful people doing really awful things.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...sters-who-knew</a><br /> <br /> I feel like this thread does a better chance of explaining how realistically frightening a supernatural creature can be beyond a mage just turning you into a frog and boiling you.<br /> <br /> As a side note in werewolf 1e its stated and implied in 2e that iron wolves, who's sacred hunt are humans. Are totally willing to assassinate politicians if they disrupt the the shadow in some way. And this isn't getting into the hunters in darkness who's entire sections tone is serial killer and for them, a subtle warning is leaving a pile of human teeth as a warning to anyone that trespasses there territory.<br /> <br /> &quot;corrupt city councilwoman? Faced with a raging Uratha in Gauru form, she\u2019s not going to do much but seize up and whimper \u2014 but with one stroke of a pen she can authorize the demolition of the tenement block that holds a pack\u2019s Locus.&quot; - Prey section for the iron wolves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 02-21-2020, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T20:34:51-08:00","id":1369499,"title":"","content":"I have GOT to admit, I am Very Tired of People putting the cart before the horse on this subject.<br /> <br /> TO wit:<br /> <br /> Lessons are not the driving force, Lessons are the result of what happens when you have this Hunger that has to be sated No Matter What and you want to at least make it useful for your fellow Kin*. It is not a culture of malevolence, it is <i>damage control</i>.<br /> <br /> *And Yes, Humanity is still your Kin, you just have a different relation than you used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T20:51:18-08:00","id":1369505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369483#post1369483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if somebody rapes your wife or kill your child to &quot;teach you a lesson,&quot; well, that shit happens in the real world. Jack the Ripper thought he was doing God's work going after prostitutes. There just seems to be some stuff in Beast that can be and has been used in the service of justifying really awful people doing really awful things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside how you're digging an even deeper hole for yourself re: I Do Not Trust You To Read This Material Cleanly\u2026<br /> <br /> Beasts concern themselves most consistently with the impact of a part of the cosmology where their reputation literally lives and dies with them \u2014 they're the Astral splat both despite and because of their default mode of activity not seeing them go on many jaunts into the dream-dimensions where art and rumor make their homes. Their particular symbolset is itself built on stuff that the human brain is evolutionarily primed to pay attention to through millions of years of fear and risk-aversion, and the closest chunks of the Astral that they deal with are the parts where ideological disputes play out as literal violent conflicts. They are monsters whose environment and sustenance are specifically social and negative.<br /> <br /> This isn't even a uniquely Begotten perspective \u2014 Kindred shape and are shaped by their prey and feeding grounds as vampires, the Uratha's ancestral duty is classically concerned overwhelmingly with steering the spiritual impact of everything that goes on in their territory, the Awakened have several different lenses with which to examine How Your Town Fucked Up, the Created foment social and physical issues in the surrounding land and populace in line with their natures, the Arisen poke at the particulars of supernatural real estate and its effect on their municipality's emotional health as a periodic distraction from their being awake making &quot;join an eternity-cult&quot; a very attractive option for most of the people they meet for more than a few days, and the Unchained routinely find themselves culpable for the breakdown or continued activity of blood-slick machinery that demands sacrifice in the name of the Devil to keep the tide from rising.<br /> <br /> Vampires and changelings (and, to a rarer extent, werewolves) need their supernatural fuel to live and have no mandate to use supernatural means to fulfill those hungers \u2014 it doesn't matter to the person getting their arm chopped off that the person who just mutilated them did it for the blood or the flesh or the raw emotion or the compelling narrative, just like it doesn't matter to the less onerous sources for <i>all of those hungers</i> to feed from that they're feeding a monster's supernatural needs by e.g. getting high and losing their wallet.<br /> <br /> This is Popular History: Bad Shit Happening is collectively memorable, and people in the public eye want to steer the way they're remembered, because that affects how their lives go \u2014 a substantial part of the definition of &quot;honor&quot; is summed up in that classic line of &quot;I have a reputation to maintain.&quot; Beasts are fixtures in the far-off fields of the Temenos, and building a legend is as much about temporal influence as it is about supernatural advancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T21:09:55-08:00","id":1369506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369483#post1369483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts feed by deliberately inflicting physical and psychological pain/terror/distress on others. If somebody gets fed on by a vampire, there's a decent chance they won't even really notice it. A bit weak/dizzy the next day? Maybe. They'll chalk it up to partying to hard and sleeping too little or something similar. The main aftereffects might be some weirdly erotic dreams about somebody wearing sunglasses after dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>See you're doing it again. You're talking a point of Vitae from a feeding as if it were all vampires do, but you're comparing it not just to a high feeding, also only Ravager despite other Hungers existing, as if the two were a one to one comparison. As opposed to the actual comparison which would be a vampire draining a person dry or to near empty leaving them hospitalized or dead. Beast doesn't have to cause physical damage, doesn't even need to force a breaking point, kindred feeding explicitly explicitly inflicts 1 lethal level of damage per vitae drained. Hell last I checked Beast at Ravenous is actually less dangerous than the comparison to a vampire at 0 Vitae since the Beast is still in control of itself. Meaning it has the options to direct its feeding or even as Heavy pointed out, wait for someone to have an exceptionally bad dream to bring you out of 0 or for the failed feedings to bring in a Hero to kill. Whereas a vampire at 0 falls to its own beast and as my ST described it <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're vitae is at 1 you're in a frenzy drinking from everything that moves. So at that point you're pretty much in NPC land and either wake up 11 vitae having drained someone dry or you don't wake up. </div> </div> </div>This is without getting into the bit that you've stated a Beast scaring someone, breaking a car window, and all that stuff is less horrible than the metaphorical date rape that vampire feeding can be compared to. This is discounting using physical force or a sneak to do it counting on the fact that a vampire bit is explicitly mentioned as overwhelmingly pleasurable to stop or if you want to bring powers into majesty and dominate can be used to bypass that pesky free-will thing in getting food.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369483#post1369483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the biggest &quot;fall down&quot; of Beast - and maybe it's greatest strength. If Mage uses Life magick to turn your into a frog then boils you and eats your frog legs, that's a pretty horrifying thing. But it's an unreal horrifying thing. Because that doesn't actually happen in the real world. But if somebody rapes your wife or kill your child to &quot;teach you a lesson,&quot; well, that shit happens in the real world. Jack the Ripper thought he was doing God's work going after prostitutes. There just seems to be some stuff in Beast that can be and has been used in the service of justifying really awful people doing really awful things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the Lancea Sanctum are totally fun like that. With the added bit about needing to convert the other kindred even if that requires torture, you forgot that bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 02-22-2020, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T23:20:13-08:00","id":1369516,"title":"","content":"I am now at the point of starting a counter for<br /> <br /> &quot;HOT TAKES: A Beast-Critic Themesplainin' their Fixes of Beast to Beast Fans!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T23:43:31-08:00","id":1369522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369516#post1369516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now at the point of starting a counter for<br /> <br /> &quot;HOT TAKES: A Beast-Critic Themesplainin' their Fixes of Beast to Beast Fans!!!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not against the idea of looking at <i>Beast </i>critically, but it's definitely odd how many people want to come into pretty much the one place where you're most likely to find fans of the game and <i>start </i>the conversation with, &quot;We all know <i>Beast </i>is bad...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T00:32:29-08:00","id":1369528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369522#post1369522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not against the idea of looking at <i>Beast </i>critically, but it's definitely odd how many people want to come into pretty much the one place where you're most likely to find fans of the game and <i>start </i>the conversation with, &quot;We all know <i>Beast </i>is bad...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And then they get surprised or offended that we disagree with their assertions or weird POVs that are tend to come off as &quot;Well of course I wouldn't trust scientists either if my assumption for normal scientist behavior was Mengela.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T07:27:54-08:00","id":1369577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369494#post1369494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts can kinda do each of those things, actually....<br /> <br /> Using the Nightmare &quot;You Must Obey&quot; absolutely lets you stare into someone's eyes and make them do your will.<br /> <br /> Merging your Lair with the area definitely turns you into a horror movie monster.<br /> <br /> Now Beasts don't have a connection to the Supernal.... But causing the gas main to explode? Hell, use Dragonfire to set the whole building on fire! You can dance amongst the flames! Pretty much the same thing.<br /> <br /> Beasts are absolutely supernatural monsters.<br /> <br /> I'm still confused as to how a vampire feeding from someone unwilling isn't a terrible thing. Feeding for a vampire is like <i>sex </i>to them. Like... Think about that. To state it more clearly, vampires often get used as rape metaphors. Werewolf: The Forsaken at least does a little better of stepping away from origins of werewolves being domestic abuser metaphors...</div> </div> </div> </div>Other beings do terrible things, but they generally do terrible <i>fictional </i>things. Frankly I'd be a whole lot happier if more of the terrible things Beasts did were fictional or otherwise required the use of supernatural traits/powers. Using Nightmares/Atavisms/etc. to pursue Feeding... it's &quot;less bad&quot; so much as &quot;less real.&quot; Like &quot;I Feed on the mean old lady who yells at kids by dragging her into a Nightmare of being alone in a shitty elder care facility to teadh her a lesson about being nice to other people instead of &quot;I feed by killing the mean old lady much loved pet cat and nailing its corpse to her front door.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess my big thing is that I play RPGs to have fun and to escape reality. I don/t really want to have my potential reaction to things the character has to do to feed be, &quot;Oh, so I need to act like my psycho ex-girlfriend or my abusive spouse?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T07:39:15-08:00","id":1369578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369577#post1369577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my big thing is that I play RPGs to have fun and to escape reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a horror game and many RPGs exist that have no purely fictional concepts in them at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don/t really want to have my potential reaction to things the character has to do to feed be, &quot;Oh, so I need to act like my psycho ex-girlfriend or my abusive spouse?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, the game has, as an entire extra facet of sustenance, &quot;tag along with one of those other monsters whose feeding methods are 'less real' and get a fixed amount of fuel from watching it happen.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-22-2020, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T07:48:31-08:00","id":1369579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369577#post1369577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my big thing is that I play RPGs to have fun and to escape reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you chose<i> Chronicles of Darkness</i> for that particular venture?<br /> <br /> Don't answer that, I don't actually care about the answer to that question. I made my peace with this sort of mentality long ago.<br /> <br /> SO let's rewind here and actually ask the question I DO keep coming back around to whenever this sort of thing pops up, be it here or the Transhumanism arguments in Promethean:<br /> <br /> Clearly something about Beast appeals to you, enough that you seemingly can't do the logically-resultant thing and just <i>find another game</i> that more easily serves your purposes (and believe me, a casual stroll through DTRPG will reveal such games), soooooooo what is it about Beast that won't let you leave but also won't let you enjoy it to properly read, contextualize, and understand it?<br /> <br /> <i>Why</i>, of all games, is Beast such a thing that you would waste your time trying to discuss rewriting it or rebooting it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-22-2020, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T14:45:37-08:00","id":1369662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369577#post1369577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other beings do terrible things, but they generally do terrible <i>fictional </i>things. Frankly I'd be a whole lot happier if more of the terrible things Beasts did were fictional or otherwise required the use of supernatural traits/powers. Using Nightmares/Atavisms/etc. to pursue Feeding... it's &quot;less bad&quot; so much as &quot;less real.&quot; Like &quot;I Feed on the mean old lady who yells at kids by dragging her into a Nightmare of being alone in a shitty elder care facility to teadh her a lesson about being nice to other people instead of &quot;I feed by killing the mean old lady much loved pet cat and nailing its corpse to her front door.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really gonna need to explain to me the difference between the result of casting a spell that lights a person on fire in a torrent of flame and the result of dousing a person in gasoline and setting them ablaze in a torrent of flame.<br /> <br /> From where I'm sitting, murder is murder. And assault is assault. Stalking is stalking.<br /> <br /> The end result here is still a burnt corpse of a person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369577#post1369577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my big thing is that I play RPGs to have fun and to escape reality. I don/t really want to have my potential reaction to things the character has to do to feed be, &quot;Oh, so I need to act like my psycho ex-girlfriend or my abusive spouse?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be very clear, Chronicles of Darkness games are games set in the horror genre. All of them. They all deal with themes and moods that are pretty serious and require mature attitudes to approach with respect for the content. Now, because the games are written pretty well, you can tweak the levers a bit here and there to either amp up the content or tone down the content.<br /> <br /> For example, there is a reason there are Hungers for Hoard, Hungers for Punishment and Hungers for Whispers and that you're ignoring them. There's a reason you're focusing so hard on Hungers for Ruin. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, though, there's an aspect to this that you're completely missing. No. Your character does NOT need to &quot;act like a psycho&quot;. You can have an entire game about a character that struggles with the morality of what their Hungers push them to want to do, refuse those hungers and try to eke out an existence otherwise through vicarious living by mingling with or stalking other supernatural entities. Or end up in a twisting spiral between Ravenous and Starving, where the sustenance they gain is only through their Horror inflicting nightmares on people, until either they work something out different, a Hero comes knocking or the character starves to death.<br /> <br /> <i><b>And this is an entirely valid game for Beast: The Primordial.</b></i><br /> <br /> That is full of personal horror and conflict that could be an amazing game to play through with someone. Chronicles of Darkness games aren't here to have a &quot;win&quot; condition, or to be about characters being &quot;awesome&quot;. If you want that (and it's FINE and GOOD to want that) go play Exalted or D&amp;D. They're perfectly good games for what they do. But Chronicles of Darkness games are about building drama, they're about horror, they're about doing uncomfortable things because it's a safe environment (or SHOULD be at your table) to get a bit dark with your role-playing and to explore the consequences of what can happen from that.<br /> <br /> Figure out what kind of game you want to play and then find a game that fits the playstyle you want to explore. If you want horror, if you want to explore a story from the point of view of a monster, then Chronicles of Darkness games have your back for that. And to note, this doesn't mean happy stories for the monsters. There is a reason there's only like... one Inheritance for Beasts that might be construed as &quot;The Good Ending&quot; (spoiler: it's not necessarily, and quite a few perspectives would view it just as hellish as the others).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T15:11:13-08:00","id":1369672,"title":"","content":"Also, even with the Hunger for Ruin it's not hard to go more abstract and fantastical. Storm Lashed Atavism, summon a level 3 or 4 extreme environment. There's nothing particularly realistic about that power, and it pretty much guarantees moderate to high satiety feeding at the cost of one satiety. Basically impossible for non supernaturals to track it back to you and even then ones without specifically investigation geared powers aren't going to have much luck.<br /> <br /> Travel the world, see interesting places, flood them. <br /> <br /> To me it increasingly seems less like you have a problem with Beast as a whole and more like a problem with some of the specific feeding examples that you continue to treat as representative of the whole.<br /> <br /> To an extent I get that. Many of those examples are pretty horrific and uncomfortable! Most of the time I make a concerted effort to think of better options for my characters. What I don't get is focusing on the examples to the point of ignoring the fact that<i> they are only examples and other less horrific options are available</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T17:41:01-08:00","id":1369707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369662#post1369662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're really gonna need to explain to me the difference between the result of casting a spell that lights a person on fire in a torrent of flame and the result of dousing a person in gasoline and setting them ablaze in a torrent of flame.<br /> <br /> From where I'm sitting, murder is murder. And assault is assault. Stalking is stalking.<br /> <br /> The end result here is still a burnt corpse of a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. One of those things is doable in the real world where we all live and the other is not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369579#post1369579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And you chose<i> Chronicles of Darkness</i> for that particular venture?<br /> <br /> Don't answer that, I don't actually care about the answer to that question. I made my peace with this sort of mentality long ago.<br /> <br /> SO let's rewind here and actually ask the question I DO keep coming back around to whenever this sort of thing pops up, be it here or the Transhumanism arguments in Promethean:<br /> <br /> Clearly something about Beast appeals to you, enough that you seemingly can't do the logically-resultant thing and just <i>find another game</i> that more easily serves your purposes (and believe me, a casual stroll through DTRPG will reveal such games), soooooooo what is it about Beast that won't let you leave but also won't let you enjoy it to properly read, contextualize, and understand it?<br /> <br /> <i>Why</i>, of all games, is Beast such a thing that you would waste your time trying to discuss rewriting it or rebooting it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I chose <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> for that particular venture? Isn't that why you chose it? After you boil out all the fat the why of this is still &quot;have fun by escaping reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for why, I really wanted to like it and I don't. I wanted to like it so much that I dropped $65.00 on the Kickstarter for it. There's parts I like. Atavisms. The Dark Mother myth. The idea of Beasts as maker of myth. The Lair. Heroes as the assholes coming to kill you for being you. But sitting at the core of it are the Hungers and the real-world asshole things you have to do to feed those Hungers. It's like somebody took a shit in my chocolate ice cream.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T17:47:34-08:00","id":1369711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369707#post1369707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. One of those things is doable in the real world where we all live and the other is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now you're just <i>choosing </i>not to listen.<br /> <br /> Why are you even bothering to continue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T18:05:26-08:00","id":1369715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369707#post1369707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But sitting at the core of it are the Hungers and the real-world asshole things you have to do to feed those Hungers. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As has been repeatedly pointed out by multiple posters: <i>You do not <u><b>have </b></u>to do those things. </i>You need to acknowledge and engage with this truth if you want anything resembling a good faith effort toward making your experience more palatable.<br /> <br /> You want to play a Beast who does fantastical monster stuff and steers away from your squicks? Great! I can give you a dozen different ways to do that! <br /> <br /> <br /> But that doesn't sound like what you want. It sounds like what you want is for the book to be rewritten so that the feeding examples are not the front and center first impression.<br /> <br /> I do get that. The tone in the core book veers all over the place and a lot of it makes for a very uncomfortable first impression. It could stand another editing pass.<br /> <br /> That wish isn't going to be granted any time soon though. What you can do now is either look past those first impressions or decide that you can't and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T18:19:37-08:00","id":1369717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369707#post1369707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. One of those things is doable in the real world where we all live and the other is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... It's not murder if a wizard does it?<br /> <br /> Okay... So... It's the <i>means </i>you find objectionable? Like, you need all the bad stuff to be of an obviously supernatural origin in order to feel comfortable engaging in it?<br /> <br /> Okay.... Okay, if I'm understanding your position right (and feel free to correct me if I'm wrong! I won't take offense to it), then there is actually a very easy fix for you, I suppose. Require any Feeding by a Beast to be done utilizing Atavisms or Nightmares. <br /> <br /> Like... There's a Nightmare that a Beast can use to kill someone, and that person turns to stone, like Medusa's Gaze. Clearly supernatural in origin, even has a fun name for it &quot;Behold, My True Form!&quot; exclamation mark included even. For Atavisms there are lots of violent options... Dragonfire for setting someone on fire in a way that is totally not doable in the real world... Basilisk's Touch as a way to make someone Drugged or Poisoned in a way that can't be done in the real world.... You can wreck a lot of structures and property to Feed Ruin using Heart of the Ocean or Storm Lashed! All done from a Supernatural Origin and completely not doable in the real world by a normal person.<br /> <br /> Does that change in approach help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T18:39:43-08:00","id":1369721,"title":"","content":"You know, I do like the idea of just once, having an actual example of what the Horror being forced to feed via nightmares from a single target without Heroic intervention looks like. To have the Begotten who refuses to 'be an arsehole' (dispute the degree of 'damage' being lower due to low Satiety) watch on as their unintentional victim breaks, slowly driven insane as Willpower and Integrity plummet under the Ravenous Horror's desperate attempt to survive.<br /> <br /> A nice little reminder that feeding is the lesser of two evils.<br /> <br /> But some people keep missing the part that the threshold 'for evil' for feeding lowers the hungrier you are. Not by Lair/Blood Potency/Primal Urge. By how long you've gone without feeding.<br /> <br /> If you need to nail a beloved pet to an old lady's door to feed, you probably don't <b><i>need</i></b> to worry about feeding. When it does get that low, wrecking her garden may be enough, if your Hunger is Ruin. Though you could just trash an arsehole's car for being a dick as easily, might even be worth more than the cat, if he loves that car.<br /> <br /> Beast has lot transgressional themes like 'damage control', 'fine lines' and 'was it worth it?' that aren't necessarily called out. But they do help contextualize the WHY of Beasts.<br /> <br /> A reminder though; within the gameworld, the supernatural is real - the only difference in the 'man on fire' example <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a> mentioned is that one suspends the player's disbelief. To the characters, they are equally real and the spell is arguebly more terrifying as it comes out of nowhere, with less chance of one getting away from the flames. If your group treats them differently that is fine, but don't assume that just because it is magic it would somehow be <b><i>less evil, horrific or morally black</i></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T18:48:05-08:00","id":1369723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369707#post1369707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I chose <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> for that particular venture? Isn't that why you chose it? After you boil out all the fat the why of this is still &quot;have fun by escaping reality.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. No. Fun is a cheap commodity I can get anywhere. Fun is a commodity I can self-produce, even. I don't go out of my way to invest time into a thread about a commodity alone for fun, nevermind the effort it takes to become a major public figure in the community of a particular commodity and even a contributor <i>to</i> that commodity simply because it's fun.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, fun's part of it, but I come for a lot more than that.<br /> <br /> And my incredulity is that Chronicles is the <i>wrong franchise</i> to &quot;escape reality&quot;. When your tagline is &quot;Our World, but with Monsters&quot;, already you have a bad premise for &quot;escaping reality&quot;, and that's before realizing that a dive of five pages into pretty much any singular book that Chronicles does not leave the concerns of reality at the door-rather the opposite, they are interested in letting you have fun <i>by</i> confronting you with that reality you somehow think you can escape from because it doesn't disrespect your intelligence or capacity to get more things than just fun from from any particular experience.<br /> <br /> Which would be a step in the reason why I bother involving myself with it in any capacity beyond merely reading the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for why, I really wanted to like it and I don't. I wanted to like it so much that I dropped $65.00 on the Kickstarter for it. There's parts I like. Atavisms. The Dark Mother myth. The idea of Beasts as maker of myth. The Lair. Heroes as the assholes coming to kill you for being you. But sitting at the core of it are the Hungers and the real-world asshole things you have to do to feed those Hungers. It's like somebody took a shit in my chocolate ice cream. </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm glad you recognize that Hungers are the dark element in the dark-grey set up of Beast.<br /> <br /> But, like.<br /> <br /> The drug-, rape-, and institutional- abuses of Requiem didn't get to you?<br /> The gang violence, use of violence for mounnity-scale or larger manipulation of society, and laissez faire attitude about murder of Forsaken didn't get to you?<br /> The consumption of the common individual-on-mass for the elites of society and the naked freedom they feel for using such however they want of Awakening didn't get to you?<br /> The emotionally driven violence of fractured individuals, open commentary on the neglected and forsaken members of society, and toxic self-identification of Created didn't get to you?<br /> The emotional and psychological manipulation of individuals, open abuse allegories, and drug abuses of Lost didn't get to you?<br /> The exploration of violence against others within the various groups, organizations, movements and classes of people in Vigil didn't get to you?<br /> The social silencing of groups, cruel employment of law, and torments rendered by obssessive individuals of Sin-Eaters didn't get to you?<br /> The correlation of brutal pre-agricultural values that grossly violate concepts of human rights and decency to actual systems in place now from Curse didn't get to you?<br /> The terrorism, open cruelties of institutional and rebel espionage organizations, and vicious manipulation of public perception to select individuals ends as expressed in Descent didn't get to you?<br /> The exploitation of individuals for economic and selfish gains, the violence that emerges from a failure to take care of our mentally and physically impaired compatriots, and exploration of how individuals and organizations turn a blind eye towards all of that from Renegades didn't get to you?<br /> <br /> And playing an opposite tact, the dedication to community building and familial care, the careful examination of both personal and societal values with an eye towards careful pruning and growth, and the self-reflections personal nature and flaws and how to own them in a way that is beneficial not just to self but to the world around you-all of that from Primodial <i>didn't get to you?</i><br /> <br /> Because here's <i>my problem</i> every time this comes up. A lot of people who make this argument <i>swear up and down</i> they've read the book, and complain that someone took a shit in their chocolate ice cream.<br /> <br /> And <i>to me</i>, it really looks like y'all ordered a coffee with a little bit of cream and sugar, and are upset when you discover it's not hot chocolate, and I <i>really have trouble</i> believing you read the menu.<br /> <br /> When your goal is to escape reality, it's not surprising that you miss the realities you run into. And unfortunately, No one can really help you with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T19:43:52-08:00","id":1369731,"title":"","content":"Sorry about that, the Escaping Reality and Shit in Chocolate Ice Cream lines lodged in my head, ANYWAYS.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369707#post1369707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's parts I like. Atavisms. The Dark Mother myth. The idea of Beasts as maker of myth. The Lair. Heroes as the assholes coming to kill you for being you.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sooooo<br /> <br /> Okay, again, my general problem here is that <i>there are other games</i> that do a lot of this. About the only one that is a sticking point is the collation of The Lair with everything else, because a lot of High Fantasy/Mythic Fantasy/Urban Fantasy/Urban Mythic/Mythic Horror/Fantasy Horror games either do mechanics in facilitation to That or to Everything else, but, like.<br /> <br /> A casual genre search on DTRPG will give you a wide variety of games that satisfactorily hit those thematic beats, mechanical execution, and even particular archetypes and structures.<br /> <br /> I <i>can</i> be sympathetic to being really invested in the language and the particulars of Primordial, and <i>really sympathetic</i> to to anyone who does want to incorporate the things that make up Lair into everything else. And answering for Not Liking Hunger when you want to enjoy those elements is hard to account for.<br /> <br /> But there are two elements I have a problem with in that sympathy.<br /> <br /> 1) Even with a distaste for it, it's not hard to see how Hunger plays a pivotal role in anchoring Beast to the themes and ideas of the rest of the Chronicles world, and the dive into optimistic humanism through the dark lens of monstrosity as a means of providing empathy and reconsideration that it generally aims for (Chronicles is generally surprisingly optimistic, but it doesn't just play at being Peppy-it goes the hard route to find realistic ways and views <i>to</i> be optimistic with), and so while a accounting for perhaps a more tasteful ground to bind Beast into the rest of the franchise while also being true to the themes and atmosphere of itself is a argument to be had, a blatant excision of that binding element without giving due to it's function is by and large fruitless.<br /> <br /> 2) Again, I kind of can't feel like there's no attempt to comprehend how an opposite angle that is in favor of Hunger in at least a general way is important or plays to the environment. Like, as a comparison, I used to <i>hate</i> Requiem 1st Edition because <i>I really hated how depressing it was</i>. (And mind you, I came in with Promethean and Changeling, so consider that). I never really failed to have meaningful conversation for other people on that because I did take the time to hear people out, reread the book with their commentary in mind, learn to adjust when I found my arguments over-inflated the actuality of the text, and really thought about how to make my point without coming accross as though it was invalid.<br /> <br /> And honestly, at the root of all that was that my dislike of the game was easily expressed by understanding that anything I liked I could crib for something else (and did for a good number of one shot games), and that honestly the element I felt worked out of it's favor was, in fact, at least working for the game on the whole as it was.<br /> <br /> Now, a lot of people complain about the way Hungers are sated in Beast, and I don't think it's unfair to have that in consideration to whether or not that's important to improving what Beast is.<br /> <br /> But the thing of the matter is a lot of people making the argument can't actually articulate a functional problem with it beyond simply not working to their taste-coffee instead of chocolate.<br /> <br /> And for <i>me-</i>I mean, I have spent a lot of my own time monkeying around with the space that Hungers occupy and the function, and things that might work outside of it. I don't want to just toss the argument out the window because other people don't have the words for it beyond their own selves. And the thing of the matter is that I just sort of think after years of wrestling with the subject is that Beast can be a better game, but it is always going be sort of niche. It has a need to be brutal and simple in order to fulfill a lot of it's goals, particularly as a crossover game, a game that sits on the dark-grey line of Chronicles' general Grey Vs Black Morality conflict and generally aims to improve our understanding of empathy for- and judgement of- people by using it's conflict of Hunger vs Kinship to humanize and demonize a lot of characters in a way a more conventional take wouldn't do, that make Hunger and the way it plays out not only functional but a vital lens for both the sort of visceral fun and complicated contemplation that it aims to create. Hungers playing out the way they do not only creates the sharpness of edge for it's kind of fun, but also brings that sharpness to the questions it asks and suggestions it guides with.<br /> <br /> No one has successfully convinced me that Hungers are not effective for the sort of game that Beast sets out to, only that the way they are presented needs to be refined to allow that function to more solidly hit and be understood within it's own context. I think Hungers are handled sloppily in presentation (in particular, it's not as neatly wrapped up in the complicated messy way it should be with Kinship, because they are the opposing forces of the game but also intimately wrapped up in each other), but not in it's core conceptual activity.<br /> <br /> And I'll be honest! Maybe I just haven't heard the right sort of argument yet! Maybe something else can absolutely fill that hole and successfully do what Beast needs to do in order to be itself.<br /> <br /> But No One arguing against it has convinced me they know how to make this a better coffee. I just keep hearing that it's not hot chocolate.<br /> <br /> TL;DR-Does no one use Chesterton's Fence anymore?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Honestly now, I'm going to start responding to a lot of hate think pieces with Chesterton's Fence now that I've thought about it. I mean, I basically have been anyways. Learn it, use it, learn from it, love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-22-2020, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T21:49:59-08:00","id":1369749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369717#post1369717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... It's not murder if a wizard does it?<br /> <br /> Okay... So... It's the <i>means </i>you find objectionable? Like, you need all the bad stuff to be of an obviously supernatural origin in order to feel comfortable engaging in it?<br /> <br /> Okay.... Okay, if I'm understanding your position right (and feel free to correct me if I'm wrong! I won't take offense to it), then there is actually a very easy fix for you, I suppose. Require any Feeding by a Beast to be done utilizing Atavisms or Nightmares.<br /> <br /> Like... There's a Nightmare that a Beast can use to kill someone, and that person turns to stone, like Medusa's Gaze. Clearly supernatural in origin, even has a fun name for it &quot;Behold, My True Form!&quot; exclamation mark included even. For Atavisms there are lots of violent options... Dragonfire for setting someone on fire in a way that is totally not doable in the real world... Basilisk's Touch as a way to make someone Drugged or Poisoned in a way that can't be done in the real world.... You can wreck a lot of structures and property to Feed Ruin using Heart of the Ocean or Storm Lashed! All done from a Supernatural Origin and completely not doable in the real world by a normal person.<br /> <br /> Does that change in approach help?</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually does. Doing that and combining it with the &quot;vicarious Feeding&quot; bit involving other supers works better for me. As things stand a &quot;medium&quot; Feeding for a Tyrant could be: Force one of your employees to have sex with you. I'm fine playing a monster, but I'd rather not play Harvey Weinstein if that makes any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:01:50-08:00","id":1369752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369749#post1369749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually does. Doing that and combining it with the &amp;quot;vicarious Feeding&amp;quot; bit involving other supers works better for me. As things stand a &amp;quot;medium&amp;quot; Feeding for a Tyrant could be: Force one of your employees to have sex with you. I'm fine playing a monster, but I'd rather not play Harvey Weinstein if that makes any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>...ok, this is a troll post clearly. <br /> <br /> Thanks for wasting everyone's time and for playing up the stereotype of Beast critics being as bad as the game they claim to make &quot;reasonable&quot; criticisms of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:16:04-08:00","id":1369755,"title":"","content":"So a thing with the Beghotten is that it is so easy to be the bad guy, not like none of the other splats can be villains with barely any effort just Beasts have it as an easy option. But, that's the thing part of the game when you play a Beast is dealing with how easy it is to just slide right into that role of monster and what are you going to do about that? So where does your character draw the line when your other half's biggest complaints about what you do to feed it are that it isn't frequent enough and that its too little? You're a Ravager, part of you looks at a place and contemplates what would upend it; you're a Predator, look at all the people and figure out who's allowed the reptile portion of their brain to doze off; a whisperer, what secrets are these people hiding and who needs confronting with someone else knowing it.<br /> <br /> The Horror doesn't care, but that's what the human part is there for. Look at the world and figure out what lines are you are willing to cross, in what situations do you feel something can or even should be done? Hell Beast has an angle I don't see that often in the reasons for a group to exist. You can easily answer the response to why they're in the group with, &quot;Because I've seen what my other half wants and I can't do that.&quot; One of the first concepts I had was predator who found the whole felt uncomfortable following their Horror's desires and the fact that they could do it, they could do it well, and that they'd might even enjoy it, so they partnered with another Beast with preferable feeding habits.<br /> <br /> By the same token so long as its in the right vein the Horror also doesn't care what you do. The Tyrant wants it to be known that others are not as great as itself. You can use your strength to beat them until they beg you to stop, you can also be that dude no one can beat in a 1 v1 basketball game to the point where everyone has just accepted that you need at least two on one against the Tyrant to even make it a good game. A Ravager can set up a bomb in a building to destroy security. My group decided to the same function could be achieved in a more entertaining way and thus was born the plan to break into a mob boss' home shave half his head, dye the other half, put cocktail shrimp in the air vents, bullion cubes in the shower head, and run his underwear up the flagpole that he didn't have in front of his house when he went to bed that night.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T22:20:24-08:00","id":1369759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369749#post1369749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As things stand a &quot;medium&quot; Feeding for a Tyrant could be: Force one of your employees to have sex with you. I'm fine playing a monster, but I'd rather not play Harvey Weinstein if that makes any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, &quot;as things stand,&quot; you don't have to play Harvey Weinstein as a Tyrant any more than you have to play Harvey Weinstein as a Ventrue or a Daeva in Vampire just because getting Vitae &quot;could be&quot; accomplished by that same method with a side of far more Uncomfortable after-effects.<br /> <br /> <i>