t doesn't make any sense to me on several levels. Like... What the fuck?<br /> <br /> But... I don't need you to explain it to me and I think I'm better off not knowing.<br /> <br /> I'm okay leaving it at that, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that hard to comprehend. Being a pretend supernatural monster is cool. Being an actual asshole human monster isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T23:21:08-08:00","id":1369771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369770#post1369770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that hard to comprehend. Being a pretend supernatural monster is cool. Being an actual asshole human monster isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong gameline.<br /> <br /> Slashers are over in Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T23:33:15-08:00","id":1369774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369770#post1369770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that hard to comprehend. Being a pretend supernatural monster is cool. Being an actual asshole human monster isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>So then the solution is to not do that thing, which the game gives you ample ability to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T23:44:02-08:00","id":1369777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369770#post1369770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that hard to comprehend. Being a pretend supernatural monster is cool. Being an actual asshole human monster isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, serious question:<br /> <br /> Do you really think that Beasts don't use their array of powers to feed?<br /> <br /> It's something that's bugged me, but others have been addressing this thread more eloquently than I tend to.<br /> <br /> But you keep asserting things that only make sense if you think Beasts have any reasons not to use their powers to feed. Beasts are supernatural monsters, no matter how human the end result of their actions. How do you think they figure out what to do to feed? Do you think they just ignore powers that would make things easier on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T00:01:26-08:00","id":1369780,"title":"","content":"Fun fact, feeding is more efficient if you used your powers, its a +1 to feed if you spent satiety. so using the power that lets you create giant stone hands to pick up all the cars parked on the side of the street and leave them upside down in nearby trees is better for your feeding than chucking a molotov into anyone's car. Added bonus, half a dozen or more cars upside down on roofs or in trees over the course of a night is gonna go viral, so there is actually potential for more opportunities to feed off the act. (And mayhaps the incident peaks the interest of some potential kin.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  rephrased for tone 02-23-2020, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T00:10:41-08:00","id":1369782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369770#post1369770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that hard to comprehend. Being a pretend supernatural monster is cool. Being an actual asshole human monster isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's the thing.... You think there's a difference. But there isn't, not really.<br /> <br /> Now... Because Beast: The Primordial can get into some heavy topics, I'm going to toss a couple useful links....<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://leavingmundania.com/2014/02/27/primer-safety-in-roleplaying-games/\" target=\"_blank\">A Primer on Safety in Roleplaying Games.<br /> <br /> S</a><a href=\"http://goldenlassogames.com/tools\" target=\"_blank\">afety Tools</a><br /> <br /> These are just a start, but there are ideas that can be very useful in helping keep things safe and sane at the table. I particularly like making use of the &quot;Rewind&quot;, &quot;Pause&quot; and &quot;Fast Forward&quot; concepts. Sometimes a scene needs to be taken back and go a different direction. Sometimes a scene just needs a &quot;Fade To Black&quot; to happen. I haven't regretted encouraging players to have more narrative control over a scene. It helps them be comfortable, it helps things stay safe. I invite players to accept &quot;Bad Things&quot; happening to their characters, but on terms they're consenting to (Like uh... &quot;And the monster shows up and does something horrible! Who wants a Beat to tell us what horrible thing the monster does and how your character reacts negatively to it?&quot;)<br /> <br /> It helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T00:24:12-08:00","id":1369784,"title":"","content":"Paradim, i truly respect your patient and polite answers: for me you are a great good example of how interact with people with very divergent opinion and dont conflate on flame war and ad personam attack.<br /> You truly seek and found a gently mediation over issue, recognizing different view without lose focus over your valid points.<br /> Thanks you, really.<br /> I want to write this and recognize your simple, honest way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T00:26:34-08:00","id":1369785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369780#post1369780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact, feeding is more efficient if you used your powers, its a +1 to feed if you spent satiety. so using the power that lets you create giant stone hands to pick up all the cars parked on the side of the street and leave them upside down in nearby trees is better for your feeding than chucking a molotov into anyone's car. Added bonus, half a dozen or more cars upside down on roofs or in trees over the course of a night is gonna go viral, so there is actually potential for more opportunities to feed off the act. (And mayhaps the incident peaks the interest of some potential kin.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonus round:<br /> <br /> 1. Most of the powers at the Begotten's disposal cost nothing to use for their base effects.<br /> <br /> 2. The Begotten Anchor Traits are &quot;way you're known to be scary \u2014 particularly when using your supernatural powers&quot; and &quot;way you act like a person that is unexpected of the usual idea of how monsters are \u2014 to put it tritely, your redeeming quality.&quot; You literally get Willpower on-demand most consistently from either being showy with your magic powers, acting mundanely in a manner appropriate to a creature of your folkloric description, or Being More Complex Than Just &quot;That Inhuman Prick.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T05:18:32-08:00","id":1369816,"title":"","content":"All right, accurately describing a problem is a necessary step to resolving it, so I'm taking another crack at this.<br /> <br /> As stated the issue is the 'abusive things you have to do', but that's clearly not accurate because you <i>don't</i> have to do those things. The game offers viable alternatives. We're still hung up on it though, so there's definitely some problem here, and I have a guess as to what it is.<br /> <br /> Is your problem that the game incentivizes, encourages, or rewards those behaviors? Because yes, it does do that, and I can see that being a deal breaker for lots of people.<br /> <br /> It's also one of the central appeals of the game. What I love about Beast is the lack of guardrails on the slippery slope of morality and the Horror looking at you with a toothy grin and a pair of skis. And the mechanically unrewarded, unincentivized freedom to say <i>And Yet I Choose To Climb</i>. When falling is so easy and so tempting choosing to take the higher, harder path means so much more. The greatest test of character isn't adversity, it's power and lack of consequences.<br /> <br /> And you can't have that without acknowledging that a fair subset are going to be horrifically abusive because it's just easier to not care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T06:36:15-08:00","id":1369827,"title":"","content":"Why is Beast so controversial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T07:37:37-08:00","id":1369833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369827#post1369827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Beast so controversial?</div> </div> </div> </div>The real root answer of this question would be a fascinating dive to explore.<br /> <br /> But the ancilliary reasons have to do with people overblowing certain elements, and with that a general commentary on the failure of proper reading habits among the masses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T07:43:32-08:00","id":1369835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369827#post1369827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Beast so controversial?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly? The roll out / kickstarter and some RPG.net discussion drift got out of hand. The actual text has never had more problems than the general CofD line. <br /> <br /> Now if you want to talk about those problems, I have a 400 page manifesto I wrote in crow blood I've been waiting to dump on the internet, but I don't think anyone cares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T07:57:46-08:00","id":1369836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369833#post1369833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the ancilliary reasons have to do with people overblowing certain elements, and with that a general commentary on the failure of proper reading habits among the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes please explain what all us knuckle dragging masses somehow missed oh great wise one.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:01:29-08:00","id":1369837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369835#post1369835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly? The roll out / kickstarter and some RPG.net discussion drift got out of hand. The actual text has never had more problems than the general CofD line.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to talk about those problems, I have a 400 page manifesto I wrote in crow blood I've been waiting to dump on the internet, but I don't think anyone cares.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if it's not a hate think piece. I love me Beast, but Heaven forbid I do know where it has issues, and would love to know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:05:56-08:00","id":1369838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369833#post1369833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the ancilliary reasons have to do with people overblowing certain elements, and with that a general commentary on the failure of proper reading habits among the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, don't do this kind of shit. The entire CofD line routinely blends flavor text meant to create an impressionistic feel with literal facts of the setting. It routinely mixes narrative abstraction mechanics that aren't meant to be used to draw fiction inferences with highly simulationist mechanics that /are/ meant to be used for fiction inferences. Flavor text and mechanics step all over each other like a junior high prom. It's composed by multiple authors with varying levels of kludge tolerance, system mastery, writing style, varying expectations/experiences for how actual play is conducted, varying awareness of other author's decisions in other books, and frequently has intentional textual ambiguities in service of an uncertain horror cosmology. The books are extremely jargon heavy and often dense with digression and throat-clearing. There are entire sections in some books devoted to explaining a single unimportant topic and single sentences that are load-bearing for absolutely core elements. The books often comment on each other, make iterative changes in response to criticism without doing so directly, and frequently require referential knowledge of other books, sometimes in other game lines. And historically, though improvements have been made, a somewhat laissez-faire attitude towards indexing, organization, editing, concision, ambiguity, error-correction, uniform terminology...<br /> <br /> &quot;Proper reading habits&quot; only make the problem worse. These books do not reward close reading. If anything, anytime I re-read one of these books I end up /more confused/ as to what the game expects. Beast is a game that was discussed in fragments before it was kickstarted, got a broad rewrite, has very important clarifying and expanding material in it's player's guide, and is a horror game that walks right into some very uncomfortable territory. Are you surprised there's some controversy about it?<br /> <br /> Now, I suppose we could blame the schools, but come on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 02-23-2020, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:36:02-08:00","id":1369841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369838#post1369838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, don't do this kind of shit. The entire CofD line routinely blends flavor text meant to create an impressionistic feel with literal facts of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not an excuse for people seeing a discussion of how symbols and narratives in the collective unconscious are Messy in the draft's section on the Temenos and concluding it meant that Beasts were allegories for oppressed minorities because the phenomenon of othering was <i>mentioned</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Proper reading habits&quot; only make the problem worse. These books do not reward close reading. If anything, anytime I re-read one of these books I end up /more confused/ as to what the game expects. </div> </div> </div>As someone who has literally had &quot;properly read the whole franchise gameline-by-gameline&quot; as an ongoing personal pursuit for the last eight years and been getting plenty of insight from it? That's on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:37:56-08:00","id":1369842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369841#post1369841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who has literally had &quot;properly read the whole franchise gameline-by-gameline&quot; as an ongoing personal pursuit for the last eight years and been getting plenty of insight from it? That's on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The CofD was the only game line I was a fan of that basically didn't survive exposure to law school. Once you're keeping an eye out for gaps in the text, they are everywhere. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:38:56-08:00","id":1369843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369838#post1369838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, don't do this kind of shit. The entire CofD line routinely blends flavor text meant to create an impressionistic feel with literal facts of the setting. It routinely mixes narrative abstraction mechanics that aren't meant to be used to draw fiction inferences with highly simulationist mechanics that /are/ meant to be used for fiction inferences. Flavor text and mechanics step all over each other like a junior high prom. It's composed by multiple authors with varying levels of kludge tolerance, system mastery, writing style, varying expectations/experiences for how actual play is conducted, varying awareness of other author's decisions in other books, and frequently has intentional textual ambiguities in service of an uncertain horror cosmology. The books are extremely jargon heavy and often dense with digression and throat-clearing. There are entire sections in some books devoted to explaining a single unimportant topic and single sentences that are load-bearing for absolutely core elements. The books often comment on each other, make iterative changes in response to criticism without doing so directly, and frequently require referential knowledge of other books, sometimes in other game lines. And historically, though improvements have been made, a somewhat laissez-faire attitude towards indexing, organization, editing, concision, ambiguity, error-correction, uniform terminology...<br /> <br /> &quot;Proper reading habits&quot; only make the problem worse. These books do not reward close reading. If anything, anytime I re-read one of these books I end up /more confused/ as to what the game expects. Beast is a game that was discussed in fragments before it was kickstarted, got a broad rewrite, has very important clarifying and expanding material in it's player's guide, and is a horror game that walks right into some very uncomfortable territory. Are you surprised there's some controversy about it?<br /> <br /> Now, I suppose we could blame the schools, but come on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've dealt with these sort of comments on these forums for....a literal decade now, not even counting my time as Being on the old forums.<br /> <br /> You're not wrong about the writing, but it also doesn't satisfactorily answer the approach to text that a lot of people have that openly cause the problems. It's true for <i>some of them</i>, but definitely not the sort of people who are in the main vein for these kinds of arguments.<br /> <br /> Now let's be clear, I actually don't blame the schools...I mean, I sort of do, but really I blame a lot more on bad faith reading, and the often shallow places such a reading comes from, often the attitudes on gaming to begin with. I'm not going to ignore, being really blunt about it, how a lot of these arguments, as much as they <i>could</i> stem from the difficulty with the text, often tend to instead emerge from an anti-intellectual perspective that treats roleplaying and engagement with text with repugnance.<br /> <br /> And it's really important that I acknowledge it because it's NOT JUST the games I like, but really part of a trend that the RPG community in general has to fight in order to make a better gaming space, because that trend is also associated <i>a lot</i> with the nastier forces that move in RPG's.<br /> <br /> So, I get why it rubs up against you, but I'm also not going to deny that it's a thing. It's a problem, a very wide one that needs to be acknowledged and addressed when these questions come up lest in continue onward due to passivity.<br /> <br /> I mean, bringing it back down to earth, how many times do I have to hear about how playing Beast is playing Harvey Weinstein and Osama Bin Laden from people who very clearly aren't actually reading the book (or at least reading it with any sense of nuance) before I can point that they're doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-23-2020, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T08:45:03-08:00","id":1369845,"title":"","content":"Oh, that's fair enough. I didn't clock you were referencing bad faith arguments specifically.<br /> <br /> That's absolutely the case with Beast. I mean a main narrative element is empathy for the non-conforming, and that is anathema to a really disruptive and nasty segment of the RPG player base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T09:52:32-08:00","id":1370077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369412#post1369412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hungry Vampire can seriously hurt or even kill people in feeding if they lose control. Maybe take out four or five in a Frenzy. A Ravenous Beast ... well, One World Trade Center was great while it lasted...</div> </div> </div> </div>A beast that goes out of control from hunger gives people bad dreams. if you're doing worse than that, its on you, especially since if you're down there, a 1 round action can feed you fine (for example: any exercise of power as a tyrant). You can also boost 1 die feedings up to 8 or so (+2 horrorspawn, +3 hunger management, +1 feeding preference, +1 in lair).<br /> <br /> All the assumptions of beasts = bad also assume there are no villains at all in the chronicle. And I don't mean &quot;lol just kill bad people.&quot; Smashing up a villain's hideout (nevermind killing people) is still good medium ruin. Simply investigating wrongdoers can be medium, at least, predator satiety. Whispers have it extremely easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T10:37:28-08:00","id":1370092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1370077#post1370077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A beast that goes out of control from hunger gives people bad dreams. if you're doing worse than that, its on you, especially since if you're down there, a 1 round action can feed you fine (for example: any exercise of power as a tyrant). You can also boost 1 die feedings up to 8 or so (+2 horrorspawn, +3 hunger management, +1 feeding preference, +1 in lair).<br /> <br /> All the assumptions of beasts = bad also assume there are no villains at all in the chronicle. And I don't mean &amp;quot;lol just kill bad people.&amp;quot; Smashing up a villain's hideout (nevermind killing people) is still good medium ruin. Simply investigating wrongdoers can be medium, at least, predator satiety. Whispers have it extremely easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>we are pretty sure John is a troll at this point. every time we tell him beast feeding do not have to be so disgustingly evil (rape) or that he CAN use supernatural powers to achieve something, he just says something more outrageous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T17:32:51-08:00","id":1370191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1369782#post1369782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Here's the thing.... You think there's a difference. But there isn't, not really.<br /> <br /> Now... Because Beast: The Primordial can get into some heavy topics, I'm going to toss a couple useful links....<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://leavingmundania.com/2014/02/27/primer-safety-in-roleplaying-games/\" target=\"_blank\">A Primer on Safety in Roleplaying Games.<br /> <br /> S</a><a href=\"http://goldenlassogames.com/tools\" target=\"_blank\">afety Tools</a><br /> <br /> These are just a start, but there are ideas that can be very useful in helping keep things safe and sane at the table. I particularly like making use of the &quot;Rewind&quot;, &quot;Pause&quot; and &quot;Fast Forward&quot; concepts. Sometimes a scene needs to be taken back and go a different direction. Sometimes a scene just needs a &quot;Fade To Black&quot; to happen. I haven't regretted encouraging players to have more narrative control over a scene. It helps them be comfortable, it helps things stay safe. I invite players to accept &quot;Bad Things&quot; happening to their characters, but on terms they're consenting to (Like uh... &quot;And the monster shows up and does something horrible! Who wants a Beat to tell us what horrible thing the monster does and how your character reacts negatively to it?&quot;)<br /> <br /> It helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate you pointing me in the direction of those. For my part it's not that Beast is a &quot;trigger&quot; so much as that it's just &quot;not my cuppa.&quot; And when I backed the Kickstarter I really thought it would be &quot;my cuppa.&quot; I don't <i>despise</i> Beast and I can see how playing a Beast would be &quot;fun&quot; for others inclined to do so (however you choose to define that word). I can also see that there are takes and tweaks that could be applied to make it more my cuppa. That all said, I've pretty much moved away from CoD, though I haven't deserted Onyx Path completely. I'm still pretty huge into Trinity Continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T17:48:10-08:00","id":1370194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1370191#post1370191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all said, I've pretty much moved away from CoD, though I haven't deserted Onyx Path completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why this thread, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T20:02:16-08:00","id":1370217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1367740-any-chance-of-a-beast-rewrite-reboot?p=1370194#post1370194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why this thread, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it'd be nice if there was a rewrite/reboot so the game would be &quot;more my cuppa.&quot; While I've moved away from CoD for now, I might well come back at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"",